#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid "Running Code Locally with Cargo"
msgstr "Menjalankan Kode secara Lokal dengan Cargo"

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid ""
"If you want to experiment with the code on your own system, then you will "
"need to first install Rust. Do this by following the [instructions in the "
"Rust Book](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch01-01-installation.html). This "
"should give you a working `rustc` and `cargo`. At the time of writing, the "
"latest stable Rust release has these version numbers:"
msgstr ""
"Jika ingin bereksperimen dengan kode di sistem sendiri, Anda perlu memasang "
"Rust terlebih dahulu. Ikuti [petunjuk dalam Rust Book](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/book/ch01-01-installation.html). Setelahnya, Anda seharusnya "
"memiliki `rustc` dan `cargo` yang bekerja. Saat tulisan ini dibuat, rilis "
"stable Rust terbaru memiliki nomor versi berikut:"

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid ""
"You can use any later version too since Rust maintains backwards "
"compatibility."
msgstr ""
"Anda juga dapat menggunakan versi yang lebih baru karena Rust mempertahankan "
"backward compatibility."

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid ""
"With this in place, follow these steps to build a Rust binary from one of the "
"examples in this training:"
msgstr ""
"Setelah persiapan selesai, ikuti langkah berikut untuk melakukan build binary "
"Rust dari salah satu contoh dalam pelatihan ini:"

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid "Click the \"Copy to clipboard\" button on the example you want to copy."
msgstr "Klik tombol “Copy to clipboard” pada contoh yang ingin disalin."

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid ""
"Use `cargo new exercise` to create a new `exercise/` directory for your code:"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan `cargo new exercise` untuk membuat direktori `exercise/` baru bagi "
"kode Anda:"

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid ""
"Navigate into `exercise/` and use `cargo run` to build and run your binary:"
msgstr ""
"Masuk ke `exercise/`, lalu gunakan `cargo run` untuk melakukan build dan "
"menjalankan binary:"

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid ""
"Replace the boilerplate code in `src/main.rs` with your own code. For "
"example, using the example on the previous page, make `src/main.rs` look like"
msgstr ""
"Ganti kode boilerplate di `src/main.rs` dengan kode Anda sendiri. Misalnya, "
"berdasarkan contoh pada halaman sebelumnya, ubah `src/main.rs` menjadi "
"seperti berikut"

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid "Use `cargo run` to build and run your updated binary:"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan `cargo run` untuk melakukan build dan menjalankan binary yang sudah "
"diperbarui:"

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid ""
"Use `cargo check` to quickly check your project for errors, use `cargo build` "
"to compile it without running it. You will find the output in `target/debug/` "
"for a normal debug build. Use `cargo build --release` to produce an optimized "
"release build in `target/release/`."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan `cargo check` untuk memeriksa error proyek dengan cepat dan `cargo "
"build` untuk mengompilasinya tanpa menjalankan. Hasil debug build biasa "
"tersedia di `target/debug/`. Gunakan `cargo build --release` untuk "
"menghasilkan release build yang dioptimalkan di `target/release/`."

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid ""
"You can add dependencies for your project by editing `Cargo.toml`. When you "
"run `cargo` commands, it will automatically download and compile missing "
"dependencies for you."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menambahkan dependency proyek dengan mengedit `Cargo.toml`. Ketika "
"menjalankan perintah `cargo`, dependency yang belum tersedia akan otomatis "
"diunduh dan dikompilasi."

#: src/cargo/running-locally.md
msgid ""
"Try to encourage the class participants to install Cargo and use a local "
"editor. It will make their life easier since they will have a normal "
"development environment."
msgstr ""
"Dorong peserta memasang Cargo dan menggunakan editor lokal. Ini akan "
"mempermudah pekerjaan mereka karena mereka memiliki lingkungan pengembangan "
"yang biasa digunakan."

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid "Welcome to Day 1"
msgstr "Selamat Datang di Hari 1"

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid ""
"This is the first day of Rust Fundamentals. We will cover a broad range of "
"topics today:"
msgstr ""
"Ini hari pertama Rust Fundamentals. Hari ini kita akan membahas beragam topik:"

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid ""
"Basic Rust syntax: variables, scalar and compound types, enums, structs, "
"references, functions, and methods."
msgstr ""
"Sintaks dasar Rust: variabel, tipe scalar dan compound, enum, struct, "
"reference, fungsi, dan method."

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid "Types and type inference."
msgstr "Tipe dan type inference."

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid "Control flow constructs: loops, conditionals, and so on."
msgstr "Konstruksi control flow: loop, conditional, dan sebagainya."

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid "User-defined types: structs and enums."
msgstr "Tipe buatan pengguna: struct dan enum."

#: src/welcome-day-1.md src/welcome-day-2.md src/welcome-day-3.md
#: src/welcome-day-4.md src/macros/welcome.md src/concurrency/welcome.md
#: src/concurrency/welcome-async.md src/idiomatic/welcome.md
msgid "Schedule"
msgstr "Jadwal"

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid ""
"Including 10 minute breaks, this session should take about 2 hours and 10 "
"minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Termasuk istirahat 10 menit, sesi ini diperkirakan membutuhkan waktu sekitar "
"2 jam dan 10 menit. Isinya:"

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid "Please remind the students that:"
msgstr "Ingatkan peserta bahwa:"

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid ""
"They should ask questions when they get them, don't save them to the end."
msgstr ""
"Mereka sebaiknya langsung bertanya saat ada pertanyaan, bukan menyimpannya "
"hingga akhir."

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid ""
"The class is meant to be interactive and discussions are very much encouraged!"
msgstr "Kelas ini dirancang interaktif dan diskusi sangat dianjurkan!"

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid ""
"As an instructor, you should try to keep the discussions relevant, i.e., keep "
"the discussions related to how Rust does things vs. some other language. It "
"can be hard to find the right balance, but err on the side of allowing "
"discussions since they engage people much more than one-way communication."
msgstr ""
"Sebagai pengajar, usahakan diskusi tetap relevan, yaitu membahas cara Rust "
"melakukan sesuatu dibandingkan bahasa lain. Menemukan keseimbangan yang tepat "
"bisa sulit. Namun, jika ragu, utamakan memberi ruang diskusi karena diskusi "
"jauh lebih melibatkan peserta daripada komunikasi satu arah."

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid ""
"The questions will likely mean that we talk about things ahead of the slides."
msgstr ""
"Pertanyaan peserta kemungkinan membuat kita membahas hal-hal yang slidenya "
"belum ditampilkan."

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid ""
"This is perfectly okay! Repetition is an important part of learning. Remember "
"that the slides are just a support and you are free to skip them as you like."
msgstr ""
"Ini tidak masalah! Pengulangan merupakan bagian penting dari belajar. Ingat "
"bahwa slide hanya alat bantu dan Anda bebas melewatinya sesuai kebutuhan."

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid ""
"The idea for the first day is to show the \"basic\" things in Rust that "
"should have immediate parallels in other languages. The more advanced parts "
"of Rust come on the subsequent days."
msgstr ""
"Hari pertama bertujuan menunjukkan hal-hal “dasar” dalam Rust yang seharusnya "
"langsung memiliki padanan dalam bahasa lain. Bagian Rust yang lebih lanjut "
"akan dibahas pada hari-hari berikutnya."

#: src/welcome-day-1.md
msgid ""
"If you're teaching this in a classroom, this is a good place to go over the "
"schedule. Note that there is an exercise at the end of each segment, followed "
"by a break. Plan to cover the exercise solution after the break. The times "
"listed here are a suggestion in order to keep the course on schedule. Feel "
"free to be flexible and adjust as necessary!"
msgstr ""
"Jika mengajar di ruang kelas, ini saat yang baik untuk menjelaskan jadwal. "
"Perhatikan bahwa setiap bagian diakhiri latihan, kemudian istirahat. "
"Rencanakan pembahasan solusi setelah istirahat. Waktu yang tercantum "
"merupakan saran agar kursus berjalan sesuai jadwal. Silakan bersikap "
"fleksibel dan sesuaikan bila diperlukan!"

