msgstr "break dan continue"

#: src/control-flow-basics.md
msgid "We will now cover the many kinds of flow control found in Rust."
msgstr "Sekarang kita akan membahas berbagai bentuk control flow dalam Rust."

#: src/control-flow-basics.md
msgid ""
"Most of this will be very familiar to what you have seen in other programming "
"languages."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian besar akan terasa sangat familier dari bahasa pemrograman lain yang "
"pernah Anda gunakan."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"A block in Rust contains a sequence of expressions, enclosed by braces `{}`."
msgstr ""
"Block dalam Rust berisi rangkaian ekspresi yang diapit kurung kurawal `{}`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"The final expression of a block determines the value and type of the whole "
"block."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi terakhir dalam block menentukan nilai dan tipe keseluruhan block."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid "// dbg!(y);\n"
msgstr "// dbg!(y);\n"

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"If the last expression ends with `;`, then the resulting value and type is "
"`()`."
msgstr ""
"Jika ekspresi terakhir diakhiri `;`, nilai dan tipe yang dihasilkan adalah "
"`()`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid "A variable's scope is limited to the enclosing block."
msgstr "Scope variabel terbatas pada block yang melingkupinya."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"You can explain that dbg! is a Rust macro that prints and returns the value "
"of a given expression for quick and dirty debugging."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menjelaskan bahwa dbg! adalah macro Rust yang mencetak dan "
"mengembalikan nilai ekspresi untuk debugging cepat dan sederhana."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"You can show how the value of the block changes by changing the last line in "
"the block. For instance, adding/removing a semicolon or using a `return`."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan bagaimana nilai block berubah ketika baris terakhirnya diubah, "
"misalnya dengan menambahkan atau menghapus titik koma, atau menggunakan "
"`return`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate that attempting to access `y` outside of its scope won't compile."
msgstr ""
"Peragakan bahwa upaya mengakses `y` di luar scope-nya tidak dapat dikompilasi."

#: src/control-flow-basics/blocks-and-scopes.md
msgid ""
"Values are effectively \"deallocated\" when they go out of their scope, even "
"if their data on the stack is still there."
msgstr ""
"Nilai secara efektif “didealokasi” ketika keluar dari scope, meskipun datanya "
"masih berada pada stack."

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "`if` expressions"
msgstr "Ekspresi `if`"

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid ""
"You use [`if` expressions](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/if-"
"expr.html#if-expressions) exactly like `if` statements in other languages:"
msgstr ""
"Anda menggunakan [ekspresi `if`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/"
"expressions/if-expr.html#if-expressions) seperti statement `if` dalam bahasa "
"lain:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"zero!\""
msgstr "\"zero!\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"biggish\""
msgstr "\"biggish\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"huge\""
msgstr "\"huge\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid ""
"In addition, you can use `if` as an expression. The last expression of each "
"block becomes the value of the `if` expression:"
msgstr ""
"Selain itu, Anda dapat menggunakan `if` sebagai ekspresi. Ekspresi terakhir "
"dari setiap block menjadi nilai ekspresi `if`:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"small\""
msgstr "\"small\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"large\""
msgstr "\"large\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid "\"number size: {}\""
msgstr "\"number size: {}\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid ""
"Because `if` is an expression and must have a particular type, both of its "
"branch blocks must have the same type. Show what happens if you add `;` after "
"`\"small\"` in the second example."
msgstr ""
"Karena `if` merupakan ekspresi dan harus memiliki tipe tertentu, kedua block "
"cabangnya harus memiliki tipe yang sama. Tunjukkan apa yang terjadi jika Anda "
"menambahkan `;` setelah `\"small\"` pada contoh kedua."

#: src/control-flow-basics/if.md
msgid ""
"An `if` expression should be used in the same way as the other expressions. "
"For example, when it is used in a `let` statement, the statement must be "
"terminated with a `;` as well. Remove the `;` before `println!` to see the "
"compiler error."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi `if` sebaiknya digunakan seperti ekspresi lain. Misalnya, ketika "
"digunakan dalam statement `let`, statement tersebut juga harus diakhiri `;`. "
"Hapus `;` sebelum `println!` untuk melihat error compiler."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "`match` can be used to check a value against one or more options:"
msgstr ""
"`match` dapat digunakan untuk memeriksa nilai terhadap satu atau beberapa "
"pilihan:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "\"one\""
msgstr "\"one\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "\"ten\""
msgstr "\"ten\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "\"one hundred\""
msgstr "\"one hundred\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "\"something else\""
msgstr "\"something else\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"Like `if` expressions, `match` also takes on the value of the branch it "
"chooses;"
msgstr ""
"Seperti ekspresi `if`, `match` juga menghasilkan nilai dari cabang yang "
"dipilih;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid "\"The value of {flag} is {val}\""
msgstr "\"The value of {flag} is {val}\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"`match` arms are evaluated from top to bottom, and the first one that matches "
"has its corresponding body executed."
msgstr ""
"Arm `match` diperiksa dari atas ke bawah. Isi arm pertama yang cocok akan "
"dijalankan."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"There is no fall-through between cases the way that `switch` works in other "
"languages."
msgstr ""
"Tidak ada fall-through antar-case seperti pada `switch` dalam bahasa lain."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"The body of a `match` arm can be a single expression or a block. Technically "
"this is the same thing, since blocks are also expressions, but students may "
"not fully understand that symmetry at this point."
msgstr ""
"Isi arm `match` dapat berupa satu ekspresi atau block. Secara teknis keduanya "
"sama karena block juga merupakan ekspresi, tetapi peserta mungkin belum "
"sepenuhnya memahami kesetaraan itu pada tahap ini."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"`match` expressions need to be exhaustive, meaning they either need to cover "
"all possible values or they need to have a default case such as `_`. "
"Exhaustiveness is easiest to demonstrate with enums, but enums haven't been "
"introduced yet. Instead we demonstrate matching on a `bool`, which is the "
"simplest primitive type."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi `match` harus exhaustive: mencakup seluruh kemungkinan nilai atau "
"memiliki default case seperti `_`. Exhaustiveness paling mudah diperagakan "
"dengan enum, tetapi enum belum diperkenalkan. Karena itu, kita memperagakan "
"pencocokan pada `bool`, tipe primitif paling sederhana."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"This slide introduces `match` without talking about pattern matching, giving "
"students a chance to get familiar with the syntax without front-loading too "
"much information. We'll be talking about pattern matching in more detail "
"tomorrow, so try not to go into too much detail here."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini memperkenalkan `match` tanpa membahas pattern matching, agar "
"peserta dapat membiasakan diri dengan sintaksnya tanpa menerima terlalu "
"banyak informasi sekaligus. Kita akan membahas pattern matching lebih "
"terperinci besok, jadi usahakan tidak membahas terlalu banyak detail di sini."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"To further motivate the usage of `match`, you can compare the examples to "
"their equivalents written with `if`. In the second case, matching on a "
"`bool`, an `if {} else {}` block is pretty similar. But in the first example "
"that checks multiple cases, a `match` expression can be more concise than `if "
"{} else if {} else if {} else`."
msgstr ""
"Untuk memperjelas manfaat `match`, bandingkan contoh dengan versi setaranya "
"menggunakan `if`. Pada contoh kedua, yaitu pencocokan `bool`, block `if {} "
"else {}` cukup serupa. Namun, pada contoh pertama yang memeriksa beberapa "
"case, ekspresi `match` dapat lebih ringkas daripada `if {} else if {} else if "
"{} else`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/match.md
msgid ""
"`match` also supports match guards, which allow you to add an arbitrary "
"logical condition that will get evaluated to determine if the match arm "
"should be taken. However talking about match guards requires explaining about "
"pattern matching, which we're trying to avoid on this slide."
msgstr ""
"`match` juga mendukung match guard untuk menambahkan kondisi logis yang "
"dievaluasi guna menentukan apakah arm tersebut dipilih. Namun, membahas match "
"guard memerlukan penjelasan pattern matching, yang sengaja belum kita bahas "
"dalam slide ini."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops.md
msgid "There are three looping keywords in Rust: `while`, `loop`, and `for`:"
msgstr "Rust memiliki tiga keyword untuk loop: `while`, `loop`, dan `for`:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops.md
msgid "`while`"
msgstr "`while`"

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops.md
msgid ""
"The [`while` keyword](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-"
"expr.html#predicate-loops) works much like in other languages, executing the "
"loop body as long as the condition is true."
msgstr ""
"[Keyword `while`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-"
"expr.html#predicate-loops) bekerja seperti dalam bahasa lain: menjalankan isi "
"loop selama kondisinya benar."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/for.md
msgid ""
"The [`for` loop](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/keyword.for.html) iterates "
"over ranges of values or the items in a collection:"
msgstr ""
"[Loop `for`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/keyword.for.html) mengiterasi "
"rentang nilai atau elemen dalam collection:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/for.md
msgid ""
"`for` loops can be given any sequence of values and will iterate through that "
"sequence."
msgstr ""
"Loop `for` dapat menerima rangkaian nilai apa pun dan akan mengiterasi "
"rangkaian tersebut."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/for.md
msgid ""
"Note that the first `for` loop only iterates to `4`. Show the `1..=5` syntax "
"for an inclusive range."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa loop `for` pertama hanya mengiterasi hingga `4`. Tunjukkan "
"sintaks `1..=5` untuk rentang inklusif."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/for.md
msgid ""
"Under the hood `for` loops use a concept called \"iterators\" to handle "
"iterating over different kinds of ranges/collections. Iterators will be "
"discussed in more detail later."
msgstr ""
"Di balik layar, loop `for` menggunakan konsep “iterator” untuk mengiterasi "
"berbagai jenis rentang/collection. Iterator akan dibahas lebih terperinci "
"nanti."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/loop.md
msgid ""
"The [`loop` expression](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/keyword.loop.html) just "
"loops forever, until a `break`."
msgstr ""
"[Ekspresi `loop`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/keyword.loop.html) terus "
"berulang hingga ada `break`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/loops/loop.md
msgid ""
"The `loop` expression works like a `while true` loop. Use it for things like "
"servers that will serve connections forever."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi `loop` bekerja seperti loop `while true`. Gunakan untuk hal seperti "
"server yang terus melayani koneksi."

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue.md
msgid ""
"If you want to immediately start the next iteration use [`continue`](https://"
"doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-expr.html#continue-expressions)."
msgstr ""
"Jika ingin langsung memulai iterasi berikutnya, gunakan [`continue`](https://"
"doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-expr.html#continue-expressions)."

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue.md
msgid ""
"If you want to exit any kind of loop early, use [`break`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-expr.html#break-expressions). With "
"`loop`, this can take an optional expression that becomes the value of the "
"`loop` expression."
msgstr ""
"Jika ingin keluar lebih awal dari jenis loop apa pun, gunakan [`break`]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/loop-expr.html#break-"
"expressions). Pada `loop`, Anda boleh menyertakan ekspresi yang menjadi nilai "
"ekspresi `loop`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue.md
msgid ""
"Note that `loop` is the only looping construct that may evaluate to a non-"
"trivial value. This is because control flow of a `loop` only proceeds to its "
"context via a `break` expression (unlike `while` and `for` loops, which can "
"also exit when the condition fails)."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `loop` adalah satu-satunya konstruksi loop yang dapat "
"menghasilkan nilai nontrivial. Sebab, control flow `loop` hanya berlanjut ke "
"konteks di luarnya melalui ekspresi `break`, berbeda dengan `while` dan `for` "
"yang juga dapat berakhir ketika kondisi tidak terpenuhi."

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue/labels.md
msgid ""
"Both `continue` and `break` can optionally take a label argument that is used "
"to break out of nested loops:"
msgstr ""
"`continue` dan `break` boleh menerima argumen label untuk mengatur "
"perpindahan keluar dari loop bersarang:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue/labels.md
msgid "Labeled break also works on arbitrary blocks, e.g."
msgstr "Break berlabel juga dapat digunakan pada block biasa, misalnya"

#: src/control-flow-basics/break-continue/labels.md
msgid "\"This line gets skipped\""
msgstr "\"This line gets skipped\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"Declaration parameters are followed by a type (the reverse of some "
"programming languages), then a return type."
msgstr ""
"Parameter dalam deklarasi diikuti tipe, berkebalikan dengan sebagian bahasa "
"pemrograman, lalu tipe nilai kembalian."

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"The last expression in a function body (or any block) becomes the return "
"value. Simply omit the `;` at the end of the expression. The `return` keyword "
"can be used for early return, but the \"bare value\" form is idiomatic at the "
"end of a function (refactor `gcd` to use a `return`)."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi terakhir dalam isi fungsi atau block apa pun menjadi nilai "
"kembalian. Cukup hilangkan `;` di akhir ekspresi. Keyword `return` dapat "
"digunakan untuk mengembalikan nilai lebih awal, tetapi bentuk “nilai "
"langsung” merupakan idiom yang umum pada akhir fungsi. Lakukan refactoring "
"pada `gcd` agar menggunakan `return`."

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"Some functions have no return value, and return the 'unit type', `()`. The "
"compiler will infer this if the return type is omitted."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian fungsi tidak memiliki nilai kembalian dan mengembalikan “unit type”, "
"`()`. Compiler akan menyimpulkannya jika tipe nilai kembalian tidak ditulis."

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"Overloading is not supported -- each function has a single implementation."
msgstr "Overloading tidak didukung—setiap fungsi memiliki satu implementasi."

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"Always takes a fixed number of parameters. Default arguments are not "
"supported. Macros can be used to support variadic functions."
msgstr ""
"Selalu menerima jumlah parameter yang tetap. Default argument tidak didukung. "
"Macro dapat digunakan untuk mendukung fungsi variadic."

#: src/control-flow-basics/functions.md
msgid ""
"Always takes a single set of parameter types. These types can be generic, "
"which will be covered later."
msgstr ""
"Selalu menerima satu himpunan tipe parameter. Tipe-tipe ini dapat bersifat "
"generic, yang akan dibahas nanti."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"Macros are expanded into Rust code during compilation, and can take a "
"variable number of arguments. They are distinguished by a `!` at the end. The "
"Rust standard library includes an assortment of useful macros."
msgstr ""
"Macro diekspansi menjadi kode Rust selama kompilasi dan dapat menerima jumlah "
"argumen yang bervariasi. Macro ditandai dengan `!` di bagian akhir. Standard "
"library Rust menyediakan berbagai macro yang berguna."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"`println!(format, ..)` prints a line to standard output, applying formatting "
"described in [`std::fmt`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fmt/index.html)."
msgstr ""
"`println!(format, ..)` mencetak satu baris ke standard output dengan format "
"yang dijelaskan dalam [`std::fmt`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/fmt/"
"index.html)."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"`format!(format, ..)` works just like `println!` but returns the result as a "
"string."
msgstr ""
"`format!(format, ..)` bekerja seperti `println!`, tetapi mengembalikan "
"hasilnya sebagai string."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid "`dbg!(expression)` logs the value of the expression and returns it."
msgstr "`dbg!(expression)` mencatat nilai ekspresi ke log dan mengembalikannya."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"`todo!()` marks a bit of code as not-yet-implemented. If executed, it will "
"panic."
msgstr ""
"`todo!()` menandai bagian kode yang belum diimplementasikan. Jika dijalankan, "
"kode tersebut akan mengalami panic."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid "\"{n}! = {}\""
msgstr "\"{n}! = {}\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"The takeaway from this section is that these common conveniences exist, and "
"how to use them. Why they are defined as macros, and what they expand to, is "
"not especially critical."
msgstr ""
"Hal utama dalam bagian ini adalah mengetahui bahwa fasilitas umum tersebut "
"tersedia dan memahami cara menggunakannya. Alasan fasilitas itu didefinisikan "
"sebagai macro dan hasil ekspansinya bukan hal yang terlalu penting di sini."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"The course does not cover defining macros, but a later section will describe "
"use of derive macros."
msgstr ""
"Kursus ini tidak membahas cara mendefinisikan macro, tetapi bagian "
"selanjutnya akan menjelaskan penggunaan derive macro."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md src/pattern-matching/match.md
#: src/idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/extension-traits/extending-other-traits.md
msgid "More To Explore"
msgstr "Untuk Dipelajari Lebih Lanjut"

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"There are a number of other useful macros provided by the standard library. "
"Some other examples you can share with students if they want to know more:"
msgstr ""
"Standard library menyediakan sejumlah macro berguna lainnya. Berikut beberapa "
"contoh yang dapat Anda bagikan jika peserta ingin mengetahui lebih lanjut:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"[`assert!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/macro.assert.html) and "
"related macros can be used to add assertions to your code. These are used "
"heavily in writing tests."
msgstr ""
"[`assert!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/macro.assert.html) dan macro "
"terkait dapat digunakan untuk menambahkan assertion ke kode. Macro ini banyak "
"digunakan saat menulis test."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"[`unreachable!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/macro.unreachable.html) "
"is used to mark a branch of control flow that should never be hit."
msgstr ""
"[`unreachable!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/macro.unreachable.html) "
"menandai cabang control flow yang seharusnya tidak pernah dicapai."

#: src/control-flow-basics/macros.md
msgid ""
"[`eprintln!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/macro.eprintln.html) "
"allows you to print to stderr."
msgstr ""
"[`eprintln!`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/macro.eprintln.html) "
"memungkinkan Anda mencetak ke stderr."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The [Collatz Sequence](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collatz_conjecture) is "
"defined as follows, for an arbitrary n<sub>1</sub> greater than zero:"
msgstr ""
"[Deret Collatz](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Collatz_conjecture) "
"didefinisikan sebagai berikut, untuk sembarang n<sub>1</sub> yang lebih besar "
"dari nol:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid ""
"If _n<sub>i</sub>_ is 1, then the sequence terminates at _n<sub>i</sub>_."
msgstr "Jika _n<sub>i</sub>_ adalah 1, deret berakhir pada _n<sub>i</sub>_."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "If _n<sub>i</sub>_ is even, then _n<sub>i+1</sub> = n<sub>i</sub> / 2_."
msgstr "Jika _n<sub>i</sub>_ genap, maka _n<sub>i+1</sub> = n<sub>i</sub> / 2_."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid ""
"If _n<sub>i</sub>_ is odd, then _n<sub>i+1</sub> = 3 * n<sub>i</sub> + 1_."
msgstr ""
"Jika _n<sub>i</sub>_ ganjil, maka _n<sub>i+1</sub> = 3 * n<sub>i</sub> + 1_."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "For example, beginning with _n<sub>1</sub>_ = 3:"
msgstr "Misalnya, dimulai dari _n<sub>1</sub>_ = 3:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "3 is odd, so _n<sub>2</sub>_ = 3 * 3 + 1 = 10;"
msgstr "3 ganjil, jadi _n<sub>2</sub>_ = 3 * 3 + 1 = 10;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "10 is even, so _n<sub>3</sub>_ = 10 / 2 = 5;"
msgstr "10 genap, jadi _n<sub>3</sub>_ = 10 / 2 = 5;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "5 is odd, so _n<sub>4</sub>_ = 3 * 5 + 1 = 16;"
msgstr "5 ganjil, jadi _n<sub>4</sub>_ = 3 * 5 + 1 = 16;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "16 is even, so _n<sub>5</sub>_ = 16 / 2 = 8;"
msgstr "16 genap, jadi _n<sub>5</sub>_ = 16 / 2 = 8;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "8 is even, so _n<sub>6</sub>_ = 8 / 2 = 4;"
msgstr "8 genap, jadi _n<sub>6</sub>_ = 8 / 2 = 4;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "4 is even, so _n<sub>7</sub>_ = 4 / 2 = 2;"
msgstr "4 genap, jadi _n<sub>7</sub>_ = 4 / 2 = 2;"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "2 is even, so _n<sub>8</sub>_ = 1; and"
msgstr "2 genap, jadi _n<sub>8</sub>_ = 1; dan"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid "the sequence terminates."
msgstr "deret berakhir."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Write a function to calculate the length of the Collatz sequence for a given "
"initial `n`."
msgstr ""
"Tulis fungsi untuk menghitung panjang deret Collatz dari nilai awal `n` yang "
"diberikan."

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid "/// Determine the length of the collatz sequence beginning at `n`.\n"
msgstr "/// Determine the length of the collatz sequence beginning at `n`.\n"

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "\"Length: {}\""
msgstr "\"Length: {}\""

#: src/control-flow-basics/exercise.md src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid "// should be 15\n"
msgstr "// should be 15\n"

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid "This solution demonstrates a few key Rust features:"
msgstr "Solusi ini menunjukkan beberapa fitur utama Rust:"

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid ""
"**`mut` arguments:** The `n` argument is declared as `mut n`. This makes the "
"local variable `n` mutable within the function scope. It does _not_ affect "
"the caller's value, as integers are `Copy` types passed by value."
msgstr ""
"**Argumen `mut`:** Argumen `n` dideklarasikan sebagai `mut n`. Ini membuat "
"variabel lokal `n` bersifat mutable dalam scope fungsi. Ini _tidak_ "
"memengaruhi nilai milik caller karena integer merupakan tipe `Copy` yang "
"diteruskan by value."

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid ""
"**`if` expressions:** Rust's `if` is an expression, meaning it produces a "
"value. We assign the result of the `if`/`else` block directly to `n`. This is "
"more concise than writing `n = ...` inside each branch."
msgstr ""
"**Ekspresi `if`:** Dalam Rust, `if` merupakan ekspresi, artinya menghasilkan "
"nilai. Kita langsung menetapkan hasil block `if`/`else` ke `n`. Ini lebih "
"ringkas daripada menulis `n = ...` pada setiap cabang."

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Implicit return:** The function ends with `len` (without a semicolon), "
"which is automatically returned."
msgstr ""
"**Implicit return:** Fungsi diakhiri `len` tanpa titik koma, yang nilainya "
"otomatis dikembalikan."

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid ""
"Note that `n` must be strictly greater than 0 for the Collatz sequence to be "
"valid. The function signature takes `i32`, but the problem description "
"implies positive integers. A more robust implementation might use `u32` or "
"return an `Option` or `Result` to handle invalid inputs (0 or negative "
"numbers), but panic or infinite loops are potential outcomes here if `n <= 0`."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `n` harus benar-benar lebih besar dari 0 agar deret Collatz "
"valid. Signature fungsi menerima `i32`, tetapi deskripsi masalah "
"mengisyaratkan integer positif. Implementasi yang lebih andal mungkin "
"menggunakan `u32` atau mengembalikan `Option` atau `Result` untuk menangani "
"input tidak valid, yaitu 0 atau angka negatif. Namun, dalam implementasi ini, "
"`n <= 0` dapat menyebabkan panic atau loop tanpa akhir."

#: src/control-flow-basics/solution.md
msgid ""
"The overflow is a potential issue if `n` grows too large, similar to the "
"Fibonacci exercise."
msgstr ""
"Overflow dapat menjadi masalah jika `n` terlalu besar, seperti pada latihan "
"Fibonacci."

#: src/welcome-day-1-afternoon.md src/welcome-day-2-afternoon.md
#: src/welcome-day-3-afternoon.md src/welcome-day-4-afternoon.md
msgid "Welcome Back"
msgstr "Selamat Datang Kembali"

#: src/welcome-day-1-afternoon.md
msgid ""
"Including 10 minute breaks, this session should take about 2 hours and 45 "
"minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Termasuk istirahat 10 menit, sesi ini diperkirakan membutuhkan waktu sekitar "
"2 jam dan 45 menit. Isinya:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays.md
msgid "This segment should take about 35 minutes. It contains:"
msgstr "Bagian ini diperkirakan membutuhkan waktu sekitar 35 menit. Isinya:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays.md
msgid ""
"We have seen how primitive types work in Rust. Now it's time for you to start "
"building new composite types."
msgstr ""
"Kita telah melihat cara kerja tipe primitif dalam Rust. Sekarang saatnya "
"mulai membuat tipe komposit baru."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"Arrays can also be initialized using the shorthand syntax, e.g. `[0; 1024]`. "
"This can be useful when you want to initialize all elements to the same "
"value, or if you have a large array that would be hard to initialize manually."
msgstr ""
"Array juga dapat diinisialisasi menggunakan sintaks singkat, misalnya `[0; "
"1024]`. Cara ini berguna ketika Anda ingin menginisialisasi semua elemen "
"dengan nilai yang sama atau ketika array berukuran besar sulit diinisialisasi "
"secara manual."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"A value of the array type `[T; N]` holds `N` (a compile-time constant) "
"elements of the same type `T`. Note that the length of the array is _part of "
"its type_, which means that `[u8; 3]` and `[u8; 4]` are considered two "
"different types. Slices, which have a size determined at runtime, are covered "
"later."
msgstr ""
"Nilai bertipe array `[T; N]` menyimpan `N` elemen dengan tipe yang sama, "
"yaitu `T`; jumlah elemennya merupakan konstanta compile-time. Perhatikan "
"bahwa panjang array merupakan _bagian dari tipenya_, sehingga `[u8; 3]` dan "
"`[u8; 4]` dianggap dua tipe berbeda. Slice, yang ukurannya ditentukan saat "
"runtime, dibahas nanti."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"Try accessing an out-of-bounds array element. The compiler is able to "
"determine that the index is unsafe, and will not compile the code:"
msgstr ""
"Coba akses elemen array di luar batas. Compiler dapat menentukan bahwa indeks "
"tersebut tidak aman dan menolak mengompilasi kodenya:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid "\"a: {a:?}\""
msgstr "\"a: {a:?}\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"Array accesses are checked at runtime. Rust optimizes these checks away when "
"possible; meaning if the compiler can prove the access is safe, it removes "
"the runtime check for better performance. They can be avoided using unsafe "
"Rust. The optimization is so good that it's hard to give an example of "
"runtime checks failing. The following code will compile but panic at runtime:"
msgstr ""
"Akses array diperiksa saat runtime. Rust menghilangkan pemeriksaan ini "
"melalui optimasi bila memungkinkan: jika compiler dapat membuktikan aksesnya "
"aman, pemeriksaan runtime dihapus untuk meningkatkan performa. Pemeriksaan "
"juga dapat dihindari menggunakan unsafe Rust. Optimasinya begitu baik "
"sehingga contoh pemeriksaan runtime yang gagal sulit dibuat. Kode berikut "
"dapat dikompilasi, tetapi akan mengalami panic saat runtime:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid "We can use literals to assign values to arrays."
msgstr "Kita dapat menggunakan literal untuk memberikan nilai pada array."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"Arrays are not heap-allocated. They are regular values with a fixed size "
"known at compile time, meaning they go on the stack. This can be different "
"from what students expect if they come from a garbage-collected language, "
"where arrays may be heap allocated by default."
msgstr ""
"Array tidak dialokasikan pada heap. Array merupakan nilai biasa dengan ukuran "
"tetap yang diketahui saat compile time, sehingga ditempatkan pada stack. Ini "
"mungkin berbeda dari perkiraan peserta yang terbiasa dengan bahasa bergarbage "
"collector, yang mungkin mengalokasikan array pada heap secara default."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"There is no way to remove elements from an array, nor add elements to an "
"array. The length of an array is fixed at compile-time, and so its length "
"cannot change at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Elemen array tidak dapat dihapus atau ditambahkan. Panjang array tetap saat "
"compile time, sehingga tidak dapat berubah saat runtime."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid "Debug Printing"
msgstr "Pencetakan untuk Debug"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"The `println!` macro asks for the debug implementation with the `?` format "
"parameter: `{}` gives the default output, `{:?}` gives the debug output. "
"Types such as integers and strings implement the default output, but arrays "
"only implement the debug output. This means that we must use debug output "
"here."
msgstr ""
"Macro `println!` menggunakan implementasi debug melalui parameter format `?`: "
"`{}` menghasilkan output default, sedangkan `{:?}` menghasilkan output debug. "
"Tipe seperti integer dan string mengimplementasikan output default, tetapi "
"array hanya mengimplementasikan output debug. Karena itu, kita harus "
"menggunakan output debug di sini."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/arrays.md
msgid ""
"Adding `#`, eg `{a:#?}`, invokes a \"pretty printing\" format, which can be "
"easier to read."
msgstr ""
"Menambahkan `#`, misalnya `{a:#?}`, menggunakan format “pretty printing” yang "
"dapat lebih mudah dibaca."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid "Like arrays, tuples have a fixed length."
msgstr "Seperti array, tuple memiliki panjang tetap."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid "Tuples group together values of different types into a compound type."
msgstr ""
"Tuple mengelompokkan nilai dengan tipe berbeda menjadi satu tipe compound."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid ""
"Fields of a tuple can be accessed by the period and the index of the value, "
"e.g. `t.0`, `t.1`."
msgstr ""
"Field tuple dapat diakses menggunakan titik dan indeks nilainya, misalnya "
"`t.0`, `t.1`."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid ""
"The empty tuple `()` is referred to as the \"unit type\" and signifies "
"absence of a meaningful value, akin to `void` in other languages."
msgstr ""
"Tuple kosong `()` disebut “unit type” dan menandakan tidak adanya nilai yang "
"bermakna, serupa dengan `void` dalam bahasa lain."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid ""
"Unlike arrays, tuples cannot be used in a `for` loop. This is because a `for` "
"loop requires all the elements to have the same type, which may not be the "
"case for a tuple."
msgstr ""
"Berbeda dari array, tuple tidak dapat digunakan dalam loop `for`. Sebab, loop "
"`for` mengharuskan semua elemen memiliki tipe yang sama, sedangkan tuple "
"belum tentu demikian."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/tuples.md
msgid ""
"There is no way to add or remove elements from a tuple. The number of "
"elements and their types are fixed at compile time and cannot be changed at "
"runtime."
msgstr ""
"Elemen tuple tidak dapat ditambahkan atau dihapus. Jumlah elemen dan tipenya "
"tetap saat compile time dan tidak dapat diubah saat runtime."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/iteration.md
msgid "The `for` statement supports iterating over arrays (but not tuples)."
msgstr "Statement `for` mendukung iterasi pada array, tetapi tidak pada tuple."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/iteration.md
msgid ""
"This functionality uses the `IntoIterator` trait, but we haven't covered that "
"yet."
msgstr ""
"Fungsionalitas ini menggunakan trait `IntoIterator`, tetapi kita belum "
"membahasnya."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/iteration.md
msgid ""
"The `assert_ne!` macro is new here. There are also `assert_eq!` and `assert!` "
"macros. These are always checked, while debug-only variants like "
"`debug_assert!` compile to nothing in release builds."
msgstr ""
"Macro `assert_ne!` baru diperkenalkan di sini. Ada pula macro `assert_eq!` "
"dan `assert!`. Ketiganya selalu diperiksa, sedangkan varian khusus debug "
"seperti `debug_assert!` tidak menghasilkan kode pada release build."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid ""
"Rust supports using pattern matching to destructure a larger value like a "
"tuple into its constituent parts:"
msgstr ""
"Rust mendukung pattern matching untuk melakukan destructuring nilai besar "
"seperti tuple menjadi bagian-bagian penyusunnya:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid "\"{tuple:?}: {}\""
msgstr "\"{tuple:?}: {}\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid "\"ordered\""
msgstr "\"ordered\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid "\"unordered\""
msgstr "\"unordered\""

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid ""
"The patterns used here are \"irrefutable\", meaning that the compiler can "
"statically verify that the value on the right of `=` has the same structure "
"as the pattern."
msgstr ""
"Pattern yang digunakan di sini bersifat “irrefutable”: compiler dapat "
"memverifikasi secara statis bahwa nilai di sebelah kanan `=` memiliki "
"struktur yang sama dengan pattern."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid ""
"A variable name is an irrefutable pattern that always matches any value, "
"hence why we can also use `let` to declare a single variable."
msgstr ""
"Nama variabel merupakan irrefutable pattern yang selalu cocok dengan nilai "
"apa pun. Karena itulah `let` juga dapat digunakan untuk mendeklarasikan satu "
"variabel."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid ""
"Rust also supports using patterns in conditionals, allowing for equality "
"comparison and destructuring to happen at the same time. This form of pattern "
"matching will be discussed in more detail later."
msgstr ""
"Rust juga mendukung penggunaan pattern dalam conditional agar perbandingan "
"kesamaan dan destructuring dapat dilakukan bersamaan. Bentuk pattern matching "
"ini dibahas lebih terperinci nanti."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/destructuring.md
msgid ""
"Edit the examples above to show the compiler error when the pattern doesn't "
"match the value being matched on."
msgstr ""
"Edit contoh di atas untuk menunjukkan error compiler ketika pattern tidak "
"cocok dengan nilai yang diperiksa."

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md
msgid "Arrays can contain other arrays:"
msgstr "Array dapat memuat array lain:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md
msgid "What is the type of this variable?"
msgstr "Apa tipe variabel ini?"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Use an array such as the above to write a function `transpose` that "
"transposes a matrix (turns rows into columns):"
msgstr ""
"Gunakan array seperti di atas untuk menulis fungsi `transpose` yang melakukan "
"transposisi matriks, yaitu mengubah baris menjadi kolom:"

#: src/tuples-and-arrays/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Copy the code below to <https://play.rust-lang.org/> and implement the "
"function. This function only operates on 3×3 matrices."
msgstr ""
"Salin kode berikut ke <https://play.rust-lang.org/> dan implementasikan "
"fungsinya. Fungsi ini hanya bekerja pada matriks 3×3."

