#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"A reference provides a way to access another value without taking ownership "
"of the value, and is also called \"borrowing\". Shared references are read-"
"only, and the referenced data cannot change."
msgstr ""
"Reference menyediakan cara mengakses nilai lain tanpa mengambil ownership "
"atas nilai tersebut; ini juga disebut “borrowing”. Shared reference bersifat "
"read-only, dan data yang dirujuk tidak dapat berubah."

#: src/references/shared.md src/std-traits/solution.md
msgid "'A'"
msgstr "'A'"

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid "'B'"
msgstr "'B'"

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"A shared reference to a type `T` has type `&T`. A reference value is made "
"with the `&` operator. The `*` operator \"dereferences\" a reference, "
"yielding its value."
msgstr ""
"Shared reference ke tipe `T` memiliki tipe `&T`. Nilai reference dibuat "
"dengan operator `&`. Operator `*` melakukan “dereference” untuk memperoleh "
"nilai yang dirujuk."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid "References can never be null in Rust, so null checking is not necessary."
msgstr ""
"Reference dalam Rust tidak pernah null, sehingga pemeriksaan null tidak "
"diperlukan."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"A reference is said to \"borrow\" the value it refers to, and this is a good "
"model for students not familiar with pointers: code can use the reference to "
"access the value, but is still \"owned\" by the original variable. The course "
"will get into more detail on ownership in day 3."
msgstr ""
"Reference dikatakan “meminjam” nilai yang dirujuknya. Ini model yang baik "
"bagi peserta yang belum mengenal pointer: kode dapat mengakses nilai melalui "
"reference, tetapi nilai tersebut tetap “dimiliki” variabel asal. Kursus ini "
"membahas ownership lebih mendalam pada hari 3."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"References are implemented as pointers, and a key advantage is that they can "
"be much smaller than the thing they point to. Students familiar with C or C++ "
"will recognize references as pointers. Later parts of the course will cover "
"how Rust prevents the memory-safety bugs that come from using raw pointers."
msgstr ""
"Reference diimplementasikan sebagai pointer. Salah satu keunggulannya adalah "
"ukurannya dapat jauh lebih kecil daripada nilai yang dirujuk. Peserta yang "
"mengenal C atau C++ akan mengenalinya sebagai pointer. Bagian selanjutnya "
"membahas cara Rust mencegah bug memory safety akibat penggunaan raw pointer."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"Explicit referencing with `&` is required, except when invoking methods, "
"where Rust performs automatic referencing and dereferencing."
msgstr ""
"Pembuatan reference secara eksplisit dengan `&` diwajibkan, kecuali saat "
"memanggil method: Rust melakukan referencing dan dereferencing secara "
"otomatis."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"Rust will auto-dereference in some cases, in particular when invoking methods "
"(try `r.is_ascii()`). There is no need for an `->` operator like in C++."
msgstr ""
"Rust melakukan auto-dereference dalam beberapa keadaan, khususnya saat "
"memanggil method; coba `r.is_ascii()`. Operator `->` seperti dalam C++ tidak "
"diperlukan."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"In this example, `r` is mutable so that it can be reassigned (`r = &b`). Note "
"that this re-binds `r`, so that it refers to something else. This is "
"different from C++, where assignment to a reference changes the referenced "
"value."
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, `r` bersifat mutable agar dapat diberi nilai baru (`r = "
"&b`). Perhatikan bahwa ini mengubah binding `r` sehingga merujuk nilai lain. "
"Ini berbeda dari C++, ketika assignment ke reference mengubah nilai yang "
"dirujuk."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"A shared reference does not allow modifying the value it refers to, even if "
"that value was mutable. Try `*r = 'X'`."
msgstr ""
"Shared reference tidak mengizinkan perubahan nilai yang dirujuk, meskipun "
"nilai itu bersifat mutable. Coba `*r = 'X'`."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"Rust is tracking the lifetimes of all references to ensure they live long "
"enough. Dangling references cannot occur in safe Rust."
msgstr ""
"Rust melacak lifetime semua reference untuk memastikan masa berlakunya cukup "
"panjang. Dangling reference tidak dapat terjadi dalam safe Rust."

#: src/references/shared.md
msgid ""
"We will talk more about borrowing and preventing dangling references when we "
"get to ownership."
msgstr ""
"Kita akan membahas borrowing dan pencegahan dangling reference lebih lanjut "
"saat membahas ownership."

#: src/references/exclusive.md
msgid ""
"Exclusive references, also known as mutable references, allow changing the "
"value they refer to. They have type `&mut T`."
msgstr ""
"Exclusive reference, yang juga disebut mutable reference, memungkinkan "
"perubahan nilai yang dirujuk. Tipenya adalah `&mut T`."

#: src/references/exclusive.md
msgid ""
"\"Exclusive\" means that only this reference can be used to access the value. "
"No other references (shared or exclusive) can exist at the same time, and the "
"referenced value cannot be accessed while the exclusive reference exists. Try "
"making an `&point.0` or changing `point.0` while `x_coord` is alive."
msgstr ""
"“Exclusive” berarti hanya reference ini yang dapat digunakan untuk mengakses "
"nilai. Reference lain, baik shared maupun exclusive, tidak boleh ada pada "
"saat yang sama, dan nilai yang dirujuk tidak dapat diakses selama exclusive "
"reference masih ada. Coba buat `&point.0` atau ubah `point.0` ketika "
"`x_coord` masih berlaku."

#: src/references/exclusive.md
msgid ""
"Be sure to note the difference between `let mut x_coord: &i32` and `let "
"x_coord: &mut i32`. The first one is a shared reference that can be bound to "
"different values, while the second is an exclusive reference to a mutable "
"value."
msgstr ""
"Pastikan Anda menjelaskan perbedaan `let mut x_coord: &i32` dan `let x_coord: "
"&mut i32`. Yang pertama adalah shared reference yang binding-nya dapat "
"diarahkan ke nilai berbeda; yang kedua adalah exclusive reference ke nilai "
"yang dapat diubah."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid "A slice gives you a view into a larger collection:"
msgstr ""
"Slice memberikan akses ke suatu bagian dari collection yang lebih besar:"

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid "Slices borrow data from the sliced type."
msgstr "Slice meminjam data dari tipe yang diambil bagiannya."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"We create a slice by borrowing `a` and specifying the starting and ending "
"indexes in brackets."
msgstr ""
"Kita membuat slice dengan meminjam `a` dan menentukan indeks awal serta akhir "
"dalam kurung siku."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"If the slice starts at index 0, Rust’s range syntax allows us to drop the "
"starting index, meaning that `&a[0..a.len()]` and `&a[..a.len()]` are "
"identical."
msgstr ""
"Jika slice dimulai dari indeks 0, sintaks rentang Rust memungkinkan kita "
"menghilangkan indeks awal. Jadi, `&a[0..a.len()]` dan `&a[..a.len()]` identik."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"The same is true for the last index, so `&a[2..a.len()]` and `&a[2..]` are "
"identical."
msgstr ""
"Hal yang sama berlaku untuk indeks akhir, sehingga `&a[2..a.len()]` dan "
"`&a[2..]` identik."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"To easily create a slice of the full array, we can therefore use `&a[..]`."
msgstr ""
"Karena itu, untuk membuat slice dari seluruh array dengan mudah, kita dapat "
"menggunakan `&a[..]`."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"`s` is a reference to a slice of `i32`s. Notice that the type of `s` "
"(`&[i32]`) no longer mentions the array length. This allows us to perform "
"computation on slices of different sizes."
msgstr ""
"`s` merupakan reference ke slice berisi nilai `i32`. Perhatikan bahwa tipe "
"`s` (`&[i32]`) tidak lagi menyebut panjang array. Dengan begitu, kita dapat "
"melakukan komputasi pada slice berukuran berbeda."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"Slices always borrow from another object. In this example, `a` has to remain "
"'alive' (in scope) for at least as long as our slice."
msgstr ""
"Slice selalu meminjam dari objek lain. Dalam contoh ini, `a` harus tetap "
"“hidup” dalam scope setidaknya selama slice kita masih berlaku."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid "You can't \"grow\" a slice once it's created:"
msgstr "Anda tidak dapat “memperbesar” slice setelah dibuat:"

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"You can't append elements of the slice, since it doesn't own the backing "
"buffer."
msgstr ""
"Anda tidak dapat menambahkan elemen ke slice karena slice tidak memiliki "
"ownership atas buffer yang mendasarinya."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"You can't grow a slice to point to a larger section of the backing buffer. A "
"slice does not have information about the length of the underlying buffer and "
"so you can't know how large the slice can be grown."
msgstr ""
"Anda tidak dapat memperbesar slice agar merujuk bagian buffer yang lebih "
"luas. Slice tidak menyimpan informasi panjang buffer yang mendasarinya, "
"sehingga Anda tidak dapat mengetahui sampai sebesar apa slice boleh "
"diperbesar."

#: src/references/slices.md
msgid ""
"To get a larger slice you have to go back to the original buffer and create a "
"larger slice from there."
msgstr ""
"Untuk memperoleh slice yang lebih besar, Anda harus kembali ke buffer asal "
"dan membuat slice yang lebih besar dari sana."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "We can now understand the two string types in Rust:"
msgstr "Sekarang kita dapat memahami dua tipe string dalam Rust:"

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "`&str` is a slice of UTF-8 encoded bytes, similar to `&[u8]`."
msgstr ""
"`&str` merupakan slice byte dengan encoding UTF-8, serupa dengan `&[u8]`."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "`String` is an owned buffer of UTF-8 encoded bytes, similar to `Vec<T>`."
msgstr ""
"`String` merupakan buffer byte dengan encoding UTF-8 yang memiliki ownership "
"atas datanya, serupa dengan `Vec<T>`."

#: src/references/strings.md src/std-traits/read-and-write.md
msgid "\"World\""
msgstr "\"World\""

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "\"s1: {s1}\""
msgstr "\"s1: {s1}\""

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "\"Hello \""
msgstr "\"Hello \""

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "\"s2: {s2}\""
msgstr "\"s2: {s2}\""

#: src/references/strings.md
