msgstr "\"s3: {s3}\""

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"`&str` introduces a string slice, which is an immutable reference to UTF-8 "
"encoded string data stored in a block of memory. String literals "
"(`\"Hello\"`), are stored in the program’s binary."
msgstr ""
"`&str` memperkenalkan string slice, yaitu immutable reference ke data string "
"dengan encoding UTF-8 yang tersimpan dalam suatu blok memori. Literal string "
"(`\"Hello\"`) disimpan dalam binary program."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"Rust's `String` type is a wrapper around a vector of bytes. As with a "
"`Vec<T>`, it is owned."
msgstr ""
"Tipe `String` dalam Rust membungkus vector byte. Seperti `Vec<T>`, tipe ini "
"memiliki ownership atas datanya."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"As with many other types `String::from()` creates a string from a string "
"literal; `String::new()` creates a new empty string, to which string data can "
"be added using the `push()` and `push_str()` methods."
msgstr ""
"Seperti pada banyak tipe lain, `String::from()` membuat string dari literal "
"string. `String::new()` membuat string kosong baru, yang dapat ditambahi data "
"string menggunakan method `push()` dan `push_str()`."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"The `format!()` macro is a convenient way to generate an owned string from "
"dynamic values. It accepts the same format specification as `println!()`."
msgstr ""
"Macro `format!()` merupakan cara praktis menghasilkan owned string dari nilai "
"dinamis. Macro ini menerima spesifikasi format yang sama dengan `println!()`."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"You can borrow `&str` slices from `String` via `&` and optionally range "
"selection. If you select a byte range that is not aligned to character "
"boundaries, the expression will panic. The `chars` iterator iterates over "
"characters and is preferred over trying to get character boundaries right."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat meminjam slice `&str` dari `String` menggunakan `&`, dengan "
"pilihan rentang bila diperlukan. Jika rentang byte yang dipilih tidak sejajar "
"dengan batas karakter, ekspresi akan mengalami panic. Iterator `chars` "
"mengiterasi karakter dan lebih disarankan daripada mencoba menentukan batas "
"karakter sendiri."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"For C++ programmers: think of `&str` as `std::string_view` from C++, but the "
"one that always points to a valid string in memory. Rust `String` is a rough "
"equivalent of `std::string` from C++ (main difference: it can only contain "
"UTF-8 encoded bytes and will never use a small-string optimization)."
msgstr ""
"Bagi programmer C++: bayangkan `&str` seperti `std::string_view` dalam C++, "
"tetapi selalu merujuk string yang valid dalam memori. `String` Rust kurang "
"lebih setara dengan `std::string` dalam C++. Perbedaan utamanya: hanya dapat "
"memuat byte dengan encoding UTF-8 dan tidak pernah menggunakan small-string "
"optimization."

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid "Byte strings literals allow you to create a `&[u8]` value directly:"
msgstr ""
"Literal byte string memungkinkan Anda membuat nilai `&[u8]` secara langsung:"

#: src/references/strings.md
msgid ""
"Raw strings allow you to create a `&str` value with escapes disabled: "
"`r\"\\n\" == \"\\\\n\"`. You can embed double-quotes by using an equal amount "
"of `#` on either side of the quotes:"
msgstr ""
"Raw string memungkinkan Anda membuat nilai `&str` tanpa pemrosesan escape: "
"`r\"\\n\" == \"\\\\n\"`. Anda dapat menyertakan tanda kutip ganda dengan "
"menggunakan jumlah `#` yang sama di kedua sisi tanda kutip:"

#: src/references/dangling.md
msgid ""
"Rust enforces a number of rules for references that make them always safe to "
"use. One rule is that references can never be `null`, making them safe to use "
"without `null` checks. The other rule we'll look at for now is that "
"references can't _outlive_ the data they point to."
msgstr ""
"Rust menerapkan sejumlah aturan agar reference selalu aman digunakan. Salah "
"satunya, reference tidak pernah `null`, sehingga aman digunakan tanpa "
"pemeriksaan `null`. Aturan lain yang kita bahas sekarang adalah bahwa "
"reference tidak boleh _berlaku lebih lama_ daripada data yang dirujuk."

#: src/references/dangling.md
msgid ""
"This slide gets students thinking about references as not simply being "
"pointers, since Rust has different rules for references than other languages."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini mengajak peserta memahami bahwa reference bukan sekadar pointer, "
"karena Rust memiliki aturan reference yang berbeda dari bahasa lain."

#: src/references/dangling.md
msgid ""
"We'll look at the rest of Rust's borrowing rules on day 3 when we talk about "
"Rust's ownership system."
msgstr ""
"Kita akan membahas aturan borrowing Rust lainnya pada hari 3 saat mempelajari "
"sistem ownership Rust."

#: src/references/dangling.md
msgid ""
"Rust's equivalent of nullability is the `Option` type, which can be used to "
"make any type \"nullable\" (not just references/pointers). We haven't yet "
"introduced enums or pattern matching, though, so try not to go into too much "
"detail about this here."
msgstr ""
"Padanan nullability dalam Rust adalah tipe `Option`, yang dapat membuat tipe "
"apa pun “nullable”, bukan hanya reference/pointer. Namun, kita belum "
"memperkenalkan enum atau pattern matching, jadi usahakan tidak membahasnya "
"terlalu terperinci di sini."

#: src/references/exercise.md
msgid ""
"We will create a few utility functions for 3-dimensional geometry, "
"representing a point as `[f64;3]`. It is up to you to determine the function "
"signatures."
msgstr ""
"Kita akan membuat beberapa fungsi bantu untuk geometri 3 dimensi, dengan "
"titik direpresentasikan sebagai `[f64;3]`. Anda menentukan sendiri signature "
"fungsinya."

