#: src/references/solution.md
msgid ""
"Note that in `normalize` we were able to do `*item /= mag` to modify each "
"element. This is because we're iterating using a mutable reference to an "
"array, which causes the `for` loop to give mutable references to each element."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa dalam `normalize`, kita dapat menggunakan `*item /= mag` "
"untuk mengubah setiap elemen. Sebab, kita mengiterasi melalui mutable "
"reference ke array, sehingga loop `for` memberikan mutable reference ke "
"setiap elemen."

#: src/references/solution.md
msgid ""
"It is also possible to take slice references here, e.g., `fn "
"magnitude(vector: &[f64]) -> f64`. This makes the function more general, at "
"the cost of a runtime length check."
msgstr ""
"Reference ke slice juga dapat digunakan di sini, misalnya `fn "
"magnitude(vector: &[f64]) -> f64`. Ini membuat fungsi lebih umum, dengan "
"konsekuensi pemeriksaan panjang saat runtime."

