#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid ""
"Newtypes are a great way to encode additional information about the value in "
"a primitive type, for example:"
msgstr ""
"Newtype merupakan cara yang sangat baik untuk menyertakan informasi tambahan "
"tentang nilai dalam tipe primitif, misalnya:"

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid "The number is measured in some units: `Newtons` in the example above."
msgstr "Angka diukur dalam satuan tertentu: `Newtons` pada contoh di atas."

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid ""
"The value passed some validation when it was created, so you no longer have "
"to validate it again at every use: `PhoneNumber(String)` or `OddNumber(u32)`."
msgstr ""
"Nilai sudah melewati validasi saat dibuat, sehingga tidak perlu divalidasi "
"lagi setiap kali digunakan: `PhoneNumber(String)` atau `OddNumber(u32)`."

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid ""
"The newtype pattern is covered extensively in the [\"Idiomatic Rust\" module]"
"(../idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md)."
msgstr ""
"Newtype pattern dibahas secara mendalam dalam [module “Idiomatic Rust”](../"
"idiomatic/leveraging-the-type-system/newtype-pattern.md)."

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate how to add a `f64` value to a `Newtons` type by accessing the "
"single field in the newtype."
msgstr ""
"Peragakan cara menambahkan nilai `f64` ke tipe `Newtons` dengan mengakses "
"satu-satunya field pada newtype."

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid ""
"Rust generally avoids implicit conversions, like automatic unwrapping or "
"using booleans as integers."
msgstr ""
"Rust umumnya menghindari konversi implisit, seperti unwrapping otomatis atau "
"penggunaan boolean sebagai integer."

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid ""
"Operator overloading is discussed on Day 2 ([Standard Library Traits](../std-"
"traits.md))."
msgstr ""
"Operator overloading dibahas pada Hari 2 ([Trait Standard Library](../std-"
"traits.md))."

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid ""
"When a tuple struct has zero fields, the `()` can be omitted. The result is a "
"zero-sized type (ZST), of which there is only one value (the name of the "
"type)."
msgstr ""
"Ketika tuple struct tidak memiliki field, `()` dapat dihilangkan. Hasilnya "
"adalah zero-sized type (ZST), yang hanya memiliki satu nilai, yaitu nama "
"tipenya."

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid ""
"This is common for types that implement some behavior but have no data "
"(imagine a `NullReader` that implements some reader behavior by always "
"returning EOF)."
msgstr ""
"Bentuk ini umum pada tipe yang mengimplementasikan perilaku tanpa memiliki "
"data. Bayangkan `NullReader` yang mengimplementasikan perilaku reader dengan "
"selalu mengembalikan EOF."

#: src/user-defined-types/tuple-structs.md
msgid ""
"The example is a subtle reference to the [Mars Climate Orbiter](https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_Climate_Orbiter) failure."
msgstr ""
"Contoh ini secara tersirat merujuk pada kegagalan [Mars Climate Orbiter]"
"(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_Climate_Orbiter)."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"The `enum` keyword allows the creation of a type which has a few different "
"variants:"
msgstr ""
"Keyword `enum` memungkinkan pembuatan tipe yang memiliki beberapa variant "
"berbeda:"

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid "// Simple variant\n"
msgstr "// Simple variant\n"

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid "// Tuple variant\n"
msgstr "// Tuple variant\n"

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid "// Struct variant\n"
msgstr "// Struct variant\n"

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid "\"On this turn: {player_move:?}\""
msgstr "\"On this turn: {player_move:?}\""

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid "Enumerations allow you to collect a set of values under one type."
msgstr ""
"Enum memungkinkan Anda mengelompokkan sejumlah nilai ke dalam satu tipe."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"`Direction` is a type with variants. There are two values of `Direction`: "
"`Direction::Left` and `Direction::Right`."
msgstr ""
"`Direction` merupakan tipe dengan variant. Ada dua nilai `Direction`: "
"`Direction::Left` dan `Direction::Right`."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"`PlayerMove` is a type with three variants. In addition to the payloads, Rust "
"will store a discriminant so that it knows at runtime which variant is in a "
"`PlayerMove` value."
msgstr ""
"`PlayerMove` merupakan tipe dengan tiga variant. Selain payload, Rust "
"menyimpan discriminant agar saat runtime dapat diketahui variant yang "
"tersimpan dalam nilai `PlayerMove`."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid "This might be a good time to compare structs and enums:"
msgstr "Ini mungkin saat yang tepat untuk membandingkan struct dan enum:"

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"In both, you can have a simple version without fields (unit struct) or one "
"with different types of fields (variant payloads)."
msgstr ""
"Pada keduanya, Anda dapat memiliki bentuk sederhana tanpa field (unit struct) "
"atau bentuk dengan field bertipe berbeda (payload variant)."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"You could even implement the different variants of an enum with separate "
"structs but then they wouldn’t be the same type as they would if they were "
"all defined in an enum."
msgstr ""
"Anda bahkan dapat mengimplementasikan setiap variant enum dengan struct "
"terpisah. Namun, hasilnya tidak lagi memiliki tipe yang sama, berbeda dari "
"ketika semuanya didefinisikan dalam satu enum."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid "Rust uses minimal space to store the discriminant."
msgstr "Rust menggunakan ruang seminimal mungkin untuk menyimpan discriminant."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid "If necessary, it stores an integer of the smallest required size"
msgstr ""
"Jika diperlukan, Rust menyimpan integer dengan ukuran terkecil yang dibutuhkan"

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"If the allowed variant values do not cover all bit patterns, it will use "
"invalid bit patterns to encode the discriminant (the \"niche optimization\"). "
"For example, `Option<&u8>` stores either a pointer to an integer or `NULL` "
"for the `None` variant."
msgstr ""
"Jika nilai variant yang diizinkan tidak mencakup seluruh pola bit, Rust "
"menggunakan pola bit yang tidak valid untuk menyimpan discriminant; ini "
"disebut “niche optimization”. Misalnya, `Option<&u8>` menyimpan pointer ke "
"integer atau `NULL` untuk variant `None`."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"You can control the discriminant if needed (e.g., for compatibility with C):"
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat mengatur discriminant jika diperlukan, misalnya untuk "
"kompatibilitas dengan C:"

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"Without `repr`, the discriminant type takes 2 bytes, because 10001 fits 2 "
"bytes."
msgstr ""
"Tanpa `repr`, tipe discriminant memerlukan 2 byte karena 10001 dapat "
"ditampung dalam 2 byte."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"Rust has several optimizations it can employ to make enums take up less space."
msgstr ""
"Rust memiliki beberapa optimasi agar enum menggunakan lebih sedikit ruang."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"Null pointer optimization: For [some types](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/"
"option/#representation), Rust guarantees that `size_of::<T>()` equals "
"`size_of::<Option<T>>()`."
msgstr ""
"Null pointer optimization: Untuk [sebagian tipe](https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"std/option/#representation), Rust menjamin bahwa `size_of::<T>()` sama dengan "
"`size_of::<Option<T>>()`."

#: src/user-defined-types/enums.md
msgid ""
"Example code if you want to show how the bitwise representation _may_ look "
"like in practice. It's important to note that the compiler provides no "
"guarantees regarding this representation, therefore this is totally unsafe."
msgstr ""
"Berikut contoh kode untuk menunjukkan bagaimana representasi bit _mungkin_ "
"terlihat dalam praktik. Perhatikan bahwa compiler tidak memberikan jaminan "
"atas representasi ini, sehingga cara ini sepenuhnya unsafe."

#: src/user-defined-types/aliases.md
msgid ""
"A type alias creates a name for another type. The two types can be used "
"interchangeably."
msgstr ""
"Type alias memberikan nama untuk tipe lain. Keduanya dapat digunakan secara "
"bergantian."

#: src/user-defined-types/aliases.md
msgid "// Aliases are more useful with long, complex types:\n"
msgstr "// Aliases are more useful with long, complex types:\n"

#: src/user-defined-types/aliases.md
msgid ""
"A [newtype](tuple-structs.html) is often a better alternative since it "
"creates a distinct type. Prefer `struct InventoryCount(usize)` to `type "
"InventoryCount = usize`."
msgstr ""
"[Newtype](tuple-structs.html) sering menjadi alternatif yang lebih baik "
"karena menghasilkan tipe yang berbeda. Utamakan `struct "
"InventoryCount(usize)` daripada `type InventoryCount = usize`."

#: src/user-defined-types/aliases.md
msgid "C programmers will recognize this as similar to a `typedef`."
msgstr ""
"Programmer C akan mengenalinya sebagai sesuatu yang mirip dengan `typedef`."

#: src/user-defined-types/const.md
msgid "`const`"
msgstr "`const`"

#: src/user-defined-types/const.md
msgid ""
"Constants are evaluated at compile time and their values are [inlined]"
"(https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/0246-const-vs-static.html) wherever they "
"are used:"
msgstr ""
"Konstanta dievaluasi saat compile time dan nilainya [disisipkan langsung]"
"(https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/0246-const-vs-static.html) di setiap tempat "
"penggunaannya:"

#: src/user-defined-types/const.md
msgid ""
"Only functions marked `const` can be called at compile time to generate "
"`const` values. `const` functions can however be called at runtime."
msgstr ""
"Hanya fungsi bertanda `const` yang dapat dipanggil saat compile time untuk "
"menghasilkan nilai `const`. Namun, fungsi `const` juga dapat dipanggil saat "
"runtime."

#: src/user-defined-types/const.md
msgid "Mention that `const` behaves semantically similar to C++'s `constexpr`"
msgstr ""
"Sampaikan bahwa secara semantik perilaku `const` serupa dengan `constexpr` "
"dalam C++"

#: src/user-defined-types/static.md
msgid "`static`"
msgstr "`static`"

#: src/user-defined-types/static.md
msgid ""
"Static variables will live during the whole execution of the program, and "
"therefore will not move:"
msgstr ""
"Variabel static berlaku selama seluruh eksekusi program, sehingga tidak akan "
"berpindah:"

#: src/user-defined-types/static.md
msgid "\"Welcome to RustOS 3.14\""
msgstr "\"Welcome to RustOS 3.14\""

#: src/user-defined-types/static.md
msgid "\"{BANNER}\""
msgstr "\"{BANNER}\""

#: src/user-defined-types/static.md
msgid ""
"As noted in the [Rust RFC Book](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/0246-const-"
"vs-static.html), these are not inlined upon use and have an actual associated "
"memory location. This is useful for unsafe and embedded code, and the "
"variable lives through the entirety of the program execution. When a globally-"
"scoped value does not have a reason to need object identity, `const` is "
"generally preferred."
msgstr ""
"Seperti dijelaskan dalam [Rust RFC Book](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/"
"0246-const-vs-static.html), variabel ini tidak disisipkan langsung saat "
"digunakan dan memiliki lokasi memori yang nyata. Ini berguna bagi kode unsafe "
"dan embedded, dan variabel berlaku selama seluruh eksekusi program. Jika "
"nilai dengan scope global tidak membutuhkan identitas objek, `const` umumnya "
"lebih disarankan."

#: src/user-defined-types/static.md
msgid "`static` is similar to mutable global variables in C++."
msgstr "`static` serupa dengan variabel global mutable dalam C++."

#: src/user-defined-types/static.md
msgid ""
"`static` provides object identity: an address in memory and state as required "
"by types with interior mutability such as `Mutex<T>`."
msgstr ""
"`static` menyediakan identitas objek: alamat dalam memori dan state yang "
"dibutuhkan tipe dengan interior mutability seperti `Mutex<T>`."

#: src/user-defined-types/static.md
msgid ""
"Because `static` variables are accessible from any thread, they must be "
"`Sync`. Interior mutability is possible through a [`Mutex`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html), atomic or similar."
msgstr ""
"Karena variabel `static` dapat diakses dari thread mana pun, variabel ini "
"harus bersifat `Sync`. Interior mutability dapat dilakukan melalui [`Mutex`]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html), atomic, atau "
"mekanisme serupa."

#: src/user-defined-types/static.md
msgid ""
"It is common to use `OnceLock` in a static as a way to support initialization "
"on first use. `OnceCell` is not `Sync` and thus cannot be used in this "
"context."
msgstr ""
"`OnceLock` umum digunakan dalam static untuk mendukung inisialisasi saat "
"pertama digunakan. `OnceCell` tidak bersifat `Sync`, sehingga tidak dapat "
"digunakan dalam konteks ini."

#: src/user-defined-types/static.md
msgid "Thread-local data can be created with the macro `std::thread_local`."
msgstr "Data thread-local dapat dibuat menggunakan macro `std::thread_local`."

#: src/user-defined-types/exercise.md
msgid ""
"We will create a data structure to represent an event in an elevator control "
"system. It is up to you to define the types and functions to construct "
"various events. Use `#[derive(Debug)]` to allow the types to be formatted "
"with `{:?}`."
msgstr ""
"Kita akan membuat struktur data untuk merepresentasikan event dalam sistem "
"kendali lift. Anda menentukan tipe dan fungsi untuk membuat berbagai event "
"tersebut. Gunakan `#[derive(Debug)]` agar tipe dapat diformat dengan `{:?}`."

#: src/user-defined-types/exercise.md
msgid ""
"This exercise only requires creating and populating data structures so that "
"`main` runs without errors. The next part of the course will cover getting "
"data out of these structures."
msgstr ""
"Latihan ini hanya mengharuskan Anda membuat dan mengisi struktur data agar "
"`main` berjalan tanpa error. Bagian selanjutnya membahas cara mengambil data "
"dari struktur tersebut."

