#: src/user-defined-types/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Enums with Data:** Rust `enum` variants can carry data. `CarArrived(Floor)` "
"carries an integer, and `ButtonPressed(Button)` carries a nested `Button` "
"enum. This allows `Event` to represent a rich set of states in a type-safe "
"way."
msgstr ""
"**Enum dengan Data:** Variant `enum` Rust dapat membawa data. "
"`CarArrived(Floor)` membawa integer, sedangkan `ButtonPressed(Button)` "
"membawa enum `Button` yang bersarang. Dengan begitu, `Event` dapat "
"merepresentasikan beragam state secara type-safe."

#: src/user-defined-types/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Type Aliases:** `type Floor = i32` gives a semantic name to `i32`. This "
"improves readability, but `Floor` is still just an `i32` to the compiler."
msgstr ""
"**Type Alias:** `type Floor = i32` memberikan nama bermakna pada `i32`. Ini "
"meningkatkan keterbacaan, tetapi bagi compiler, `Floor` tetap merupakan `i32`."

#: src/user-defined-types/solution.md
msgid ""
"**`#[derive(Debug)]`:** We use this attribute to automatically generate code "
"to format the enums for printing with `{:?}`. Without this, we would have to "
"manually implement the `fmt::Debug` trait."
msgstr ""
"**`#[derive(Debug)]`:** Kita menggunakan atribut ini untuk otomatis "
"menghasilkan kode pemformatan enum agar dapat dicetak dengan `{:?}`. "
"Tanpanya, kita harus mengimplementasikan trait `fmt::Debug` secara manual."

#: src/user-defined-types/solution.md
msgid ""
"**Nested Enums:** The `Button` enum is nested inside `Event::ButtonPressed`. "
"This hierarchical structure is common in Rust for modeling complex domains."
msgstr ""
"**Enum Bersarang:** Enum `Button` bersarang di dalam `Event::ButtonPressed`. "
"Struktur hierarkis ini umum digunakan dalam Rust untuk memodelkan domain "
"kompleks."

#: src/user-defined-types/solution.md
msgid ""
"Note that `Event::CarDoorOpened` is a \"unit variant\" (it carries no data), "
"while `Event::CarArrived` is a \"tuple variant\"."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `Event::CarDoorOpened` adalah “unit variant” yang tidak "
"membawa data, sedangkan `Event::CarArrived` adalah “tuple variant”."

#: src/user-defined-types/solution.md
msgid ""
"You might discuss why `Button` is a separate enum rather than just having "
"`LobbyCallButtonPressed` and `CarFloorButtonPressed` variants on `Event`. "
"Both are valid, but grouping related concepts (like buttons) can make the "
"code cleaner."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat membahas alasan `Button` menjadi enum terpisah, alih-alih sekadar "
"menambahkan variant `LobbyCallButtonPressed` dan `CarFloorButtonPressed` pada "
"`Event`. Keduanya valid, tetapi pengelompokan konsep terkait, seperti tombol, "
"dapat membuat kode lebih rapi."

