#: src/pattern-matching/infallible.md
msgid ""
"All of the demonstrated patterns are _irrefutable_, meaning that they will "
"always match the value on the right hand side."
msgstr ""
"Semua pattern yang diperagakan bersifat _irrefutable_, artinya selalu cocok "
"dengan nilai di sebelah kanan."

#: src/pattern-matching/infallible.md
msgid ""
"Patterns are type-specific, including irrefutable patterns. Try adding or "
"removing an element to the tuple and look at the resulting compiler errors."
msgstr ""
"Pattern bergantung pada tipe, termasuk irrefutable pattern. Coba tambahkan "
"atau hapus satu elemen tuple, lalu perhatikan error compiler yang muncul."

#: src/pattern-matching/infallible.md
msgid ""
"Variable names are patterns that always match and bind the matched value into "
"a new variable with that name."
msgstr ""
"Nama variabel merupakan pattern yang selalu cocok dan mengikat nilai yang "
"cocok ke variabel baru dengan nama tersebut."

#: src/pattern-matching/infallible.md
msgid ""
"`_` is a pattern that always matches any value, discarding the matched value."
msgstr ""
"`_` merupakan pattern yang selalu cocok dengan nilai apa pun dan mengabaikan "
"nilai tersebut."

#: src/pattern-matching/infallible.md
msgid "`..` allows you to ignore multiple values at once."
msgstr "`..` memungkinkan Anda mengabaikan beberapa nilai sekaligus."

#: src/pattern-matching/infallible.md
msgid ""
"You can also demonstrate more advanced usages of `..`, such as ignoring the "
"middle elements of a tuple."
msgstr ""
"Anda juga dapat memperagakan penggunaan `..` yang lebih lanjut, seperti "
"mengabaikan elemen-elemen di tengah tuple."

#: src/pattern-matching/infallible.md
msgid "All of these patterns work with arrays as well:"
msgstr "Semua pattern ini juga dapat digunakan pada array:"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"The `match` keyword lets you match a value against one or more _patterns_. "
"The patterns can be simple values, similarly to `switch` in C and C++, but "
"they can also be used to express more complex conditions:"
msgstr ""
"Keyword `match` memungkinkan Anda mencocokkan nilai dengan satu atau beberapa "
"_pattern_. Pattern dapat berupa nilai sederhana, seperti pada `switch` dalam "
"C dan C++, tetapi juga dapat menyatakan kondisi yang lebih kompleks:"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "'x'"
msgstr "'x'"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "'q'"
msgstr "'q'"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "\"Quitting\""
msgstr "\"Quitting\""

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "'s'"
msgstr "'s'"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "'w'"
msgstr "'w'"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "'d'"
msgstr "'d'"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "\"Moving around\""
msgstr "\"Moving around\""

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "'0'"
msgstr "'0'"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "'9'"
msgstr "'9'"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "\"Number input\""
msgstr "\"Number input\""

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "\"Lowercase: {key}\""
msgstr "\"Lowercase: {key}\""

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "\"Something else\""
msgstr "\"Something else\""

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"A variable in the pattern (`key` in this example) will create a binding that "
"can be used within the match arm. We will learn more about this on the next "
"slide."
msgstr ""
"Variabel dalam pattern, yaitu `key` pada contoh ini, membuat binding yang "
"dapat digunakan dalam match arm. Kita membahasnya lebih lanjut pada slide "
"berikutnya."

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"A match guard causes the arm to match only if the condition is true. If the "
"condition is false the match will continue checking later cases."
msgstr ""
"Match guard membuat arm hanya cocok jika kondisinya benar. Jika kondisi "
"salah, pencocokan dilanjutkan ke case berikutnya."

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"You might point out how some specific characters are being used when in a "
"pattern"
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menjelaskan penggunaan beberapa karakter khusus dalam pattern"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "`|` as an `or`"
msgstr "`|` sebagai `or`"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "`..` matches any number of items"
msgstr "`..` mencocokkan sejumlah elemen berapa pun"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "`1..=5` represents an inclusive range"
msgstr "`1..=5` menyatakan rentang inklusif"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "`_` is a wild card"
msgstr "`_` merupakan wildcard"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"Match guards as a separate syntax feature are important and necessary when we "
"wish to concisely express more complex ideas than patterns alone would allow."
msgstr ""
"Match guard sebagai fitur sintaks tersendiri penting dan diperlukan ketika "
"kita ingin menyatakan gagasan yang lebih kompleks secara ringkas, melebihi "
"kemampuan pattern saja."

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"Match guards are different from `if` expressions after the `=>`. An `if` "
"expression is evaluated after the match arm is selected. Failing the `if` "
"condition inside of that block won't result in other arms of the original "
"`match` expression being considered. In the following example, the wildcard "
"pattern `_ =>` is never even attempted."
msgstr ""
"Match guard berbeda dari ekspresi `if` setelah `=>`. Ekspresi `if` dievaluasi "
"setelah match arm dipilih. Jika kondisi `if` dalam block itu tidak terpenuhi, "
"arm lain dalam ekspresi `match` asal tidak akan diperiksa. Dalam contoh "
"berikut, pattern wildcard `_ =>` bahkan tidak pernah dicoba."

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "\"Uppercase\""
msgstr "\"Uppercase\""

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "\"Bug: this is never printed\""
msgstr "\"Bug: this is never printed\""

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"The condition defined in the guard applies to every expression in a pattern "
"with an `|`."
msgstr ""
"Kondisi dalam guard berlaku untuk setiap ekspresi pada pattern yang "
"menggunakan `|`."

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"Note that you can't use an existing variable as the condition in a match arm, "
"as it will instead be interpreted as a variable name pattern, which creates a "
"new variable that will shadow the existing one. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa Anda tidak dapat menggunakan variabel yang sudah ada sebagai "
"kondisi dalam match arm. Variabel itu justru ditafsirkan sebagai pattern nama "
"variabel, yang membuat variabel baru dan melakukan shadowing terhadap "
"variabel lama. Contohnya:"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "\"Expected value is 5, actual is {expected}\""
msgstr "\"Expected value is 5, actual is {expected}\""

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "\"Value was something else\""
msgstr "\"Value was something else\""

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"Here we're trying to match on the number 123, where we want the first case to "
"check if the value is 5. The naive expectation is that the first case won't "
"match because the value isn't 5, but instead this is interpreted as a "
"variable pattern which always matches, meaning the first branch will always "
"be taken. If a constant is used instead this will then work as expected."
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita mencoba mencocokkan angka 123 dan ingin case pertama memeriksa "
"apakah nilainya 5. Sekilas, case pertama seharusnya tidak cocok karena "
"nilainya bukan 5. Namun, bentuk ini ditafsirkan sebagai pattern variabel yang "
"selalu cocok, sehingga cabang pertama selalu dipilih. Jika menggunakan "
"konstanta, perilakunya sesuai harapan."

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"Another piece of pattern syntax you can show students is the `@` syntax which "
"binds a part of a pattern to a variable. For example:"
msgstr ""
"Sintaks pattern lain yang dapat diperagakan adalah `@`, yang mengikat "
"sebagian pattern ke variabel. Contohnya:"

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid "\"outer: {outer:?}, inner: {inner}\""
msgstr "\"outer: {outer:?}, inner: {inner}\""

#: src/pattern-matching/match.md
msgid ""
"In this example `inner` has the value 123 which it pulled from the `Option` "
"via destructuring, `outer` captures the entire `Some(inner)` expression, so "
"it contains the full `Option::Some(123)`. This is rarely used but can be "
"useful in more complex patterns."
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, `inner` bernilai 123 yang diambil dari `Option` melalui "
"destructuring. Sementara itu, `outer` menangkap seluruh ekspresi "
"`Some(inner)`, sehingga memuat `Option::Some(123)` secara utuh. Bentuk ini "
"jarang digunakan, tetapi dapat berguna dalam pattern yang lebih kompleks."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid "Structs"
msgstr "Struct"

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid "Like tuples, structs can also be destructured by matching:"
msgstr "Seperti tuple, struct juga dapat di-destructure melalui pencocokan:"

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid "\"Standing still\""
msgstr "\"Standing still\""

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid "\"{repeat} step x: {x}\""
msgstr "\"{repeat} step x: {x}\""

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid "\"Single step y: {y}\""
msgstr "\"Single step y: {y}\""

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid "\"Other move\""
msgstr "\"Other move\""

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid "Change the literal values in `m` to match with the other patterns."
msgstr "Ubah nilai literal dalam `m` agar cocok dengan pattern lain."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid "Add a new field to `Movement` and make changes to the pattern as needed."
msgstr ""
"Tambahkan field baru ke `Movement` dan sesuaikan pattern bila diperlukan."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid "Note how `delta: (x, 0)` is a nested pattern."
msgstr "Perhatikan bahwa `delta: (x, 0)` merupakan pattern bersarang."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid ""
"Try `match &m` and check the type of captures. The pattern syntax remains the "
"same, but the captures become shared references. This is [match ergonomics]"
"(https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/2005-match-ergonomics.html) and is often "
"useful with `match self` when implementing methods on an enum."
msgstr ""
"Coba `match &m` dan periksa tipe nilai yang ditangkap. Sintaks pattern tetap "
"sama, tetapi hasil tangkapannya menjadi shared reference. Ini disebut [match "
"ergonomics](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/2005-match-ergonomics.html) dan "
"sering berguna pada `match self` saat mengimplementasikan method pada enum."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid ""
"The same effect occurs with `match &mut m`: the captures become exclusive "
"references."
msgstr ""
"Efek serupa terjadi pada `match &mut m`: hasil tangkapannya menjadi exclusive "
"reference."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-structs.md
msgid ""
"The distinction between a capture and a constant expression can be hard to "
"spot. Try changing the `0` in the first arm to a variable, and see that it "
"subtly doesn't work. Change it to a `const` and see it working again."
msgstr ""
"Perbedaan antara nilai tangkapan dan ekspresi konstan bisa sulit terlihat. "
"Coba ganti `0` pada arm pertama dengan variabel dan perhatikan bahwa "
"perilakunya berubah secara halus sehingga tidak lagi bekerja sebagaimana "
"mestinya. Ganti dengan `const` dan lihat bahwa perilakunya kembali sesuai."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid "Like tuples, enums can also be destructured by matching:"
msgstr "Seperti tuple, enum juga dapat di-destructure melalui pencocokan:"

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid ""
"Patterns can also be used to bind variables to parts of your values. This is "
"how you inspect the structure of your types. Let us start with a simple "
"`enum` type:"
msgstr ""
"Pattern juga dapat digunakan untuk mengikat variabel ke bagian-bagian nilai. "
"Dengan cara ini, Anda memeriksa struktur tipe. Mari mulai dengan tipe `enum` "
"sederhana:"

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid "\"cannot divide {n} into two equal parts\""
msgstr "\"cannot divide {n} into two equal parts\""

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid "\"{n} divided in two is {half}\""
msgstr "\"{n} divided in two is {half}\""

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid "\"sorry, an error happened: {msg}\""
msgstr "\"sorry, an error happened: {msg}\""

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid ""
"Here we have used the arms to _destructure_ the `Result` value. In the first "
"arm, `half` is bound to the value inside the `Ok` variant. In the second arm, "
"`msg` is bound to the error message."
msgstr ""
"Di sini, kita menggunakan arm untuk melakukan _destructuring_ nilai `Result`. "
"Pada arm pertama, `half` terikat pada nilai dalam variant `Ok`. Pada arm "
"kedua, `msg` terikat pada pesan error."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid ""
"The `if`/`else` expression is returning an enum that is later unpacked with a "
"`match`."
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi `if`/`else` mengembalikan enum yang kemudian diuraikan menggunakan "
"`match`."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid ""
"You can try adding a third variant to the enum definition and displaying the "
"errors when running the code. Point out the places where your code is now "
"inexhaustive and how the compiler tries to give you hints."
msgstr ""
"Coba tambahkan variant ketiga pada definisi enum, lalu tampilkan error saat "
"kode dijalankan. Tunjukkan bagian kode yang kini tidak exhaustive dan cara "
"compiler memberikan petunjuk."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid ""
"The values in the enum variants can only be accessed after being pattern "
"matched."
msgstr ""
"Nilai dalam variant enum hanya dapat diakses setelah dicocokkan menggunakan "
"pattern."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate what happens when the search is inexhaustive. Note the advantage "
"the Rust compiler provides by confirming when all cases are handled."
msgstr ""
"Peragakan apa yang terjadi ketika pencocokan tidak exhaustive. Tunjukkan "
"manfaat compiler Rust yang memastikan seluruh case telah ditangani."

#: src/pattern-matching/destructuring-enums.md
msgid ""
"Demonstrate the syntax for a struct-style variant by adding one to the enum "
"definition and the `match`. Point out how this is syntactically similar to "
"matching on a struct."
msgstr ""
"Peragakan sintaks variant bergaya struct dengan menambahkannya pada definisi "
"enum dan `match`. Tunjukkan kemiripan sintaksnya dengan pencocokan struct."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow.md
msgid ""
"Rust has a few control flow constructs that differ from other languages. They "
"are used for pattern matching:"
msgstr ""
"Rust memiliki beberapa konstruksi control flow yang berbeda dari bahasa lain. "
"Konstruksi ini digunakan untuk pattern matching:"

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow.md
msgid "`if let` expressions"
msgstr "Ekspresi `if let`"

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow.md
msgid "`while let` expressions"
msgstr "Ekspresi `while let`"

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow.md
msgid "`let else` expressions"
msgstr "Ekspresi `let else`"

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/if-let.md
msgid ""
"The [`if let` expression](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/if-"
"expr.html#if-let-expressions) lets you execute different code depending on "
"whether a value matches a pattern:"
msgstr ""
"[Ekspresi `if let`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/expressions/if-"
"expr.html#if-let-expressions) memungkinkan Anda menjalankan kode berbeda "
"berdasarkan kecocokan nilai dengan pattern:"

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/if-let.md
msgid "\"slept for {duration:?}\""
msgstr "\"slept for {duration:?}\""

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/if-let.md
msgid ""
"Unlike `match`, `if let` does not have to cover all branches. This can make "
"it more concise than `match`."
msgstr ""
"Berbeda dari `match`, `if let` tidak harus mencakup seluruh cabang. Karena "
"itu, bentuknya dapat lebih ringkas daripada `match`."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/if-let.md
msgid "A common usage is handling `Some` values when working with `Option`."
msgstr ""
"Salah satu penggunaan yang umum adalah menangani nilai `Some` saat "
"menggunakan `Option`."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/if-let.md
msgid ""
"Unlike `match`, `if let` does not support guard clauses for pattern matching."
msgstr ""
"Berbeda dari `match`, `if let` tidak mendukung guard clause untuk pattern "
"matching."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/if-let.md
msgid "With an `else` clause, this can be used as an expression."
msgstr "Dengan klausa `else`, bentuk ini dapat digunakan sebagai ekspresi."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/while-let.md
msgid ""
"Like with `if let`, there is a [`while let`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"reference/expressions/loop-expr.html#predicate-pattern-loops) variant that "
"repeatedly tests a value against a pattern:"
msgstr ""
"Serupa dengan `if let`, ada varian [`while let`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"reference/expressions/loop-expr.html#predicate-pattern-loops) yang berulang "
"kali memeriksa nilai terhadap pattern:"

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/while-let.md
msgid "\"Comprehensive Rust 🦀\""
msgstr "\"Comprehensive Rust 🦀\""

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/while-let.md
msgid "// (There are more efficient ways to reverse a string!)\n"
msgstr "// (There are more efficient ways to reverse a string!)\n"

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/while-let.md
msgid ""
"Here [`String::pop`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/string/"
"struct.String.html#method.pop) returns `Some(c)` until the string is empty, "
"after which it will return `None`. The `while let` lets us keep iterating "
"through all items."
msgstr ""
"Di sini, [`String::pop`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/string/"
"struct.String.html#method.pop) mengembalikan `Some(c)` hingga string kosong, "
"lalu mengembalikan `None`. Dengan `while let`, kita dapat terus mengiterasi "
"seluruh elemen."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/while-let.md
msgid ""
"Point out that the `while let` loop will keep going as long as the value "
"matches the pattern."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan bahwa loop `while let` terus berjalan selama nilainya cocok dengan "
"pattern."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/while-let.md
msgid ""
"You could rewrite the `while let` loop as an infinite loop with an if "
"statement that breaks when there is no value to unwrap for `name.pop()`. The "
"`while let` provides syntactic sugar for the above scenario."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat menulis ulang loop `while let` sebagai loop tanpa akhir dengan "
"statement if yang menghentikannya ketika `name.pop()` tidak menghasilkan "
"nilai untuk di-unwrap. `while let` menyediakan syntactic sugar untuk situasi "
"tersebut."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/while-let.md
msgid ""
"This form cannot be used as an expression, because it may have no value if "
"the condition is false."
msgstr ""
"Bentuk ini tidak dapat digunakan sebagai ekspresi karena mungkin tidak "
"memiliki nilai jika kondisinya salah."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/let-else.md
msgid "`let else` Statements"
msgstr "Statement `let else`"

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/let-else.md
msgid ""
"For the common case of matching a pattern and returning from the function, "
"use [`let else`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/flow_control/"
"let_else.html). The \"else\" case must diverge (`return`, `break`, or panic - "
"anything but falling off the end of the block)."
msgstr ""
"Untuk kasus umum ketika Anda mencocokkan pattern dan keluar dari fungsi, "
"gunakan [`let else`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/rust-by-example/flow_control/"
"let_else.html). Cabang “else” harus diverge, misalnya dengan `return`, "
"`break`, atau panic; alurnya tidak boleh sekadar mencapai akhir block."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/let-else.md
msgid "\"got None\""
msgstr "\"got None\""

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/let-else.md
msgid "\"got empty string\""
msgstr "\"got empty string\""

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/let-else.md
msgid "\"not a hex digit\""
msgstr "\"not a hex digit\""

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/let-else.md
msgid "\"result: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"result: {:?}\""

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/let-else.md
#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md src/testing/solution.md src/android/testing.md
#: src/android/testing/googletest.md
msgid "\"foo\""
msgstr "\"foo\""

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/let-else.md
msgid ""
"This early return-based control flow is common in Rust error handling code, "
"where you try to get a value out of a `Result`, returning an error if the "
"`Result` was `Err`."
msgstr ""
"Control flow berbasis early return ini umum pada kode error handling Rust: "
"Anda mencoba mengambil nilai dari `Result` dan mengembalikan error jika "
"`Result` berupa `Err`."

#: src/pattern-matching/let-control-flow/let-else.md
msgid ""
"If students ask, you can also demonstrate how real error handling code would "
"be written with `?`."
msgstr ""
"Jika peserta bertanya, peragakan juga cara menulis kode error handling yang "
"sebenarnya menggunakan `?`."

