msgstr "\"Monaco Grand Prix\""

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid "// race.add_lap(42);\n"
msgstr "// race.add_lap(42);\n"

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"The `self` arguments specify the \"receiver\" - the object the method acts "
"on. There are several common receivers for a method:"
msgstr ""
"Argumen `self` menentukan “receiver”, yaitu objek tempat method bekerja. Ada "
"beberapa bentuk receiver yang umum:"

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"`&self`: borrows the object from the caller using a shared and immutable "
"reference. The object can be used again afterwards."
msgstr ""
"`&self`: meminjam objek dari caller menggunakan reference yang shared dan "
"immutable. Objek dapat digunakan kembali setelahnya."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"`&mut self`: borrows the object from the caller using a unique and mutable "
"reference. The object can be used again afterwards."
msgstr ""
"`&mut self`: meminjam objek dari caller menggunakan reference yang unik dan "
"mutable. Objek dapat digunakan kembali setelahnya."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"`self`: takes ownership of the object and moves it away from the caller. The "
"method becomes the owner of the object. The object will be dropped "
"(deallocated) when the method returns, unless its ownership is explicitly "
"transmitted. Complete ownership does not automatically mean mutability."
msgstr ""
"`self`: mengambil ownership objek dan memindahkannya dari caller. Method "
"menjadi pemilik objek. Objek akan di-drop (didealokasi) saat method selesai, "
"kecuali ownership-nya diteruskan secara eksplisit. Ownership penuh tidak "
"otomatis berarti mutability."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid "`mut self`: same as above, but the method can mutate the object."
msgstr "`mut self`: sama seperti di atas, tetapi method dapat mengubah objek."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"No receiver: this becomes a static method on the struct. Typically used to "
"create constructors that are called `new` by convention."
msgstr ""
"Tanpa receiver: fungsi menjadi static method pada struct. Biasanya digunakan "
"untuk membuat constructor yang secara konvensi dinamai `new`."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid "It can be helpful to introduce methods by comparing them to functions."
msgstr ""
"Memperkenalkan method dengan membandingkannya terhadap fungsi dapat membantu."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"Methods are called on an instance of a type (such as a struct or enum), the "
"first parameter represents the instance as `self`."
msgstr ""
"Method dipanggil pada instance suatu tipe, seperti struct atau enum. "
"Parameter pertama merepresentasikan instance tersebut sebagai `self`."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"Developers may choose to use methods to take advantage of method receiver "
"syntax and to help keep them more organized. By using methods we can keep all "
"the implementation code in one predictable place."
msgstr ""
"Developer dapat memilih method untuk memanfaatkan sintaks receiver dan "
"membantu menata kode. Dengan method, seluruh kode implementasi dapat "
"diletakkan pada satu tempat yang mudah diperkirakan."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"Note that methods can also be called like associated functions by explicitly "
"passing the receiver in, e.g. `CarRace::add_lap(&mut race, 20)`."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa method juga dapat dipanggil seperti associated function "
"dengan meneruskan receiver secara eksplisit, misalnya `CarRace::add_lap(&mut "
"race, 20)`."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid "Point out the use of the keyword `self`, a method receiver."
msgstr "Tunjukkan penggunaan keyword `self` sebagai receiver method."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"Show that it is an abbreviated term for `self: Self` and perhaps show how the "
"struct name could also be used."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan bahwa bentuk ini merupakan singkatan dari `self: Self`. Anda juga "
"dapat memperagakan penggunaan nama struct sebagai penggantinya."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"Explain that `Self` is a type alias for the type the `impl` block is in and "
"can be used elsewhere in the block."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan bahwa `Self` merupakan type alias bagi tipe yang menjadi sasaran "
"block `impl` dan dapat digunakan di bagian lain dalam block tersebut."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"Note how `self` is used like other structs and dot notation can be used to "
"refer to individual fields."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `self` digunakan seperti struct lain, dan notasi titik dapat "
"digunakan untuk mengakses setiap field."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"This might be a good time to demonstrate how the `&self` differs from `self` "
"by trying to run `finish` twice."
msgstr ""
"Ini mungkin saat yang tepat untuk memperagakan perbedaan `&self` dan `self` "
"dengan mencoba menjalankan `finish` dua kali."

#: src/methods-and-traits/methods.md
msgid ""
"Beyond variants on `self`, there are also [special wrapper types](https://"
"doc.rust-lang.org/reference/special-types-and-traits.html) allowed to be "
"receiver types, such as `Box<Self>`."
msgstr ""
"Selain variasi `self`, beberapa [tipe wrapper khusus](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/reference/special-types-and-traits.html), seperti `Box<Self>`, juga "
"diizinkan sebagai tipe receiver."

#: src/methods-and-traits/traits.md
msgid ""
"Rust lets you abstract over types with traits. They're similar to interfaces:"
msgstr ""
"Rust memungkinkan abstraksi atas berbagai tipe melalui trait. Trait serupa "
"dengan interface:"

#: src/methods-and-traits/traits.md
msgid "/// Return a sentence from this pet.\n"
msgstr "/// Return a sentence from this pet.\n"

#: src/methods-and-traits/traits.md
msgid "/// Print a string to the terminal greeting this pet.\n"
msgstr "/// Print a string to the terminal greeting this pet.\n"

#: src/methods-and-traits/traits.md
msgid ""
"A trait defines a number of methods that types must have in order to "
"implement the trait."
msgstr ""
"Trait mendefinisikan sejumlah method yang harus dimiliki suatu tipe agar "
"dapat mengimplementasikan trait tersebut."

#: src/methods-and-traits/traits.md
msgid ""
"In the \"Generics\" segment, next, we will see how to build functionality "
"that is generic over all types implementing a trait."
msgstr ""
"Pada bagian “Generics” berikutnya, kita melihat cara membuat fungsionalitas "
"yang bersifat generic untuk semua tipe yang mengimplementasikan suatu trait."

