#: src/generics/generic-functions.md
msgid ""
"Rust supports generics, which lets you abstract algorithms or data structures "
"(such as sorting or a binary tree) over the types used or stored."
msgstr ""
"Rust mendukung generics, yang memungkinkan algoritma atau struktur data, "
"seperti sorting atau binary tree, diabstraksikan terhadap tipe yang digunakan "
"atau disimpan."

#: src/generics/generic-functions.md
msgid "\"picked a number: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"picked a number: {:?}\""

#: src/generics/generic-functions.md
msgid "\"picked a string: {:?}\""
msgstr "\"picked a string: {:?}\""

#: src/generics/generic-functions.md
msgid "'L'"
msgstr "'L'"

#: src/generics/generic-functions.md
msgid "'R'"
msgstr "'R'"

#: src/generics/generic-functions.md
msgid ""
"It can be helpful to show the monomorphized versions of `pick`, either before "
"talking about the generic `pick` in order to show how generics can reduce "
"code duplication, or after talking about generics to show how "
"monomorphization works."
msgstr ""
"Menunjukkan versi `pick` hasil monomorphization dapat membantu. Peragakan "
"sebelum membahas `pick` generic untuk menunjukkan cara generics mengurangi "
"duplikasi kode, atau setelahnya untuk menjelaskan cara kerja monomorphization."

#: src/generics/generic-functions.md
msgid ""
"Rust infers a type for T based on the types of the arguments and return value."
msgstr ""
"Rust menyimpulkan tipe untuk T berdasarkan tipe argumen dan nilai kembalian."

#: src/generics/generic-functions.md
msgid ""
"In this example we only use the primitive types `i32` and `char` for `T`, but "
"we can use any type here, including user-defined types:"
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, kita hanya menggunakan tipe primitif `i32` dan `char` untuk "
"`T`. Namun, tipe apa pun dapat digunakan di sini, termasuk tipe buatan "
"pengguna:"

#: src/generics/generic-functions.md
msgid ""
"This is similar to C++ templates, but Rust partially compiles the generic "
"function immediately, so that function must be valid for all types matching "
"the constraints. For example, try modifying `pick` to return `left + right` "
"if `cond` is false. Even if only the `pick` instantiation with integers is "
"used, Rust still considers it invalid. C++ would let you do this."
msgstr ""
"Ini serupa dengan template C++, tetapi Rust langsung mengompilasi sebagian "
"fungsi generic, sehingga fungsi harus valid untuk semua tipe yang memenuhi "
"batasannya. Misalnya, coba ubah `pick` agar mengembalikan `left + right` jika "
"`cond` salah. Meski hanya instansiasi `pick` dengan integer yang digunakan, "
"Rust tetap menganggapnya tidak valid. C++ mengizinkan hal ini."

#: src/generics/generic-functions.md
msgid ""
"Generic code is turned into non-generic code based on the call sites. This is "
"a zero-cost abstraction: you get exactly the same result as if you had hand-"
"coded the data structures without the abstraction."
msgstr ""
"Kode generic diubah menjadi kode non-generic berdasarkan tempat "
"pemanggilannya. Ini merupakan zero-cost abstraction: hasilnya persis sama "
"seperti jika Anda menulis struktur data tersebut secara manual tanpa "
"abstraksi."

#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid ""
"When working with generics, you often want to require the types to implement "
"some trait, so that you can call this trait's methods."
msgstr ""
"Saat menggunakan generics, Anda sering ingin mengharuskan tipe "
"mengimplementasikan trait tertentu agar method trait tersebut dapat dipanggil."

#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "You can do this with `T: Trait`:"
msgstr "Gunakan `T: Trait` untuk melakukannya:"

#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "\"{pair:?}\""
msgstr "\"{pair:?}\""

#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "Try making a `NotCloneable` and passing it to `duplicate`."
msgstr "Coba buat `NotCloneable` dan teruskan ke `duplicate`."

#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "When multiple traits are necessary, use `+` to join them."
msgstr "Jika beberapa trait diperlukan, gabungkan menggunakan `+`."

#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "Show a `where` clause, students will encounter it when reading code."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan klausa `where` karena peserta akan menjumpainya saat membaca kode."

#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "It declutters the function signature if you have many parameters."
msgstr "Klausa ini merapikan signature fungsi yang memiliki banyak parameter."

#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid "It has additional features making it more powerful."
msgstr "Klausa ini juga memiliki fitur tambahan yang membuatnya lebih andal."

#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid ""
"If someone asks, the extra feature is that the type on the left of \":\" can "
"be arbitrary, like `Option<T>`."
msgstr ""
"Jika ada yang bertanya, fitur tambahan itu memungkinkan tipe di sebelah kiri "
"\":\" berupa tipe apa pun, seperti `Option<T>`."

#: src/generics/trait-bounds.md
msgid ""
"Note that Rust does not (yet) support specialization. For example, given the "
"original `duplicate`, it is invalid to add a specialized `duplicate(a: u32)`."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa Rust belum mendukung specialization. Misalnya, jika "
"`duplicate` asli sudah ada, menambahkan versi khusus `duplicate(a: u32)` "
"tidak valid."

#: src/generics/generic-data.md
msgid ""
"You can use generics to abstract over the concrete field type. Returning to "
"the exercise for the previous segment:"
msgstr ""
"Generics dapat digunakan untuk mengabstraksikan tipe konkret field. Mari "
"kembali ke latihan pada bagian sebelumnya:"

#: src/generics/generic-data.md src/closures/exercise.md
#: src/closures/solution.md
msgid "\"[stderr] verbosity={verbosity}: {message}\""
msgstr "\"[stderr] verbosity={verbosity}: {message}\""

#: src/generics/generic-data.md src/closures/exercise.md
#: src/closures/solution.md
msgid "\"[stdout] verbosity={verbosity}: {message}\""
msgstr "\"[stdout] verbosity={verbosity}: {message}\""

#: src/generics/generic-data.md
msgid ""
"_Q:_ Why is `L` specified twice in `impl<L: Logger> .. VerbosityFilter<L>`? "
"Isn't that redundant?"
msgstr ""
"_Tanya:_ Mengapa `L` ditulis dua kali pada `impl<L: Logger> .. "
"VerbosityFilter<L>`? Bukankah itu berlebihan?"

#: src/generics/generic-data.md
msgid ""
"This is because it is a generic implementation section for generic type. They "
"are independently generic."
msgstr ""
"Sebab, bagian implementasinya bersifat generic dan ditujukan untuk tipe "
"generic. Keduanya bersifat generic secara terpisah."

#: src/generics/generic-data.md
msgid "It means these methods are defined for any `L`."
msgstr "Artinya, method-method ini didefinisikan untuk `L` apa pun."

#: src/generics/generic-data.md
msgid "It is possible to write `impl VerbosityFilter<StderrLogger> { .. }`."
msgstr "Anda dapat menulis `impl VerbosityFilter<StderrLogger> { .. }`."

#: src/generics/generic-data.md
msgid ""
"`VerbosityFilter` is still generic and you can use `VerbosityFilter<f64>`, "
"but methods in this block will only be available for "
"`VerbosityFilter<StderrLogger>`."
msgstr ""
"`VerbosityFilter` tetap generic dan Anda dapat menggunakan "
"`VerbosityFilter<f64>`, tetapi method dalam block ini hanya tersedia untuk "
"`VerbosityFilter<StderrLogger>`."

#: src/generics/generic-data.md
msgid ""
"Note that we don't put a trait bound on the `VerbosityFilter` type itself. "
"You can put bounds there as well, but generally in Rust we only put the trait "
"bounds on the impl blocks."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa kita tidak memberi trait bound pada tipe `VerbosityFilter` "
"itu sendiri. Bound juga dapat diletakkan di sana, tetapi dalam Rust kita "
"umumnya hanya meletakkan trait bound pada block impl."

#: src/generics/generic-traits.md
msgid ""
"Traits can also be generic, just like types and functions. A trait's "
"parameters get concrete types when it is used. For example the [`From<T>`]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/trait.From.html) trait is used to "
"define type conversions:"
msgstr ""
"Trait juga dapat bersifat generic, seperti tipe dan fungsi. Parameter trait "
"memperoleh tipe konkret saat digunakan. Misalnya, trait [`From<T>`](https://"
"doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/trait.From.html) digunakan untuk mendefinisikan "
"konversi tipe:"

#: src/generics/generic-traits.md
msgid "\"Converted from integer: {from}\""
msgstr "\"Converted from integer: {from}\""

#: src/generics/generic-traits.md
msgid "\"Converted from bool: {from}\""
msgstr "\"Converted from bool: {from}\""

#: src/generics/generic-traits.md
msgid ""
"The `From` trait will be covered later in the course, but its [definition in "
"the `std` docs](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/trait.From.html) is "
"simple, and copied here for reference."
msgstr ""
"Trait `From` dibahas nanti, tetapi [definisinya dalam dokumentasi `std`]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/trait.From.html) sederhana dan disalin "
"di sini sebagai rujukan."

#: src/generics/generic-traits.md
msgid ""
"Implementations of the trait do not need to cover all possible type "
"parameters. Here, `Foo::from(\"hello\")` would not compile because there is "
"no `From<&str>` implementation for `Foo`."
msgstr ""
"Implementasi trait tidak harus mencakup semua kemungkinan parameter tipe. Di "
"sini, `Foo::from(\"hello\")` tidak dapat dikompilasi karena tidak ada "
"implementasi `From<&str>` untuk `Foo`."

#: src/generics/generic-traits.md
msgid ""
"Generic traits take types as \"input\", while associated types are a kind of "
"\"output\" type. A trait can have multiple implementations for different "
"input types."
msgstr ""
"Trait generic menerima tipe sebagai “input”, sedangkan associated type "
"merupakan semacam tipe “output”. Satu trait dapat memiliki beberapa "
"implementasi untuk tipe input yang berbeda."

#: src/generics/generic-traits.md
msgid ""
"In fact, Rust requires that at most one implementation of a trait match for "
"any type T. Unlike some other languages, Rust has no heuristic for choosing "
"the \"most specific\" match. There is work on adding this support, called "
"[specialization](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/1210-impl-"
"specialization.html)."
msgstr ""
"Rust sebenarnya mengharuskan paling banyak satu implementasi trait yang cocok "
"untuk setiap tipe T. Berbeda dari beberapa bahasa lain, Rust tidak memiliki "
"heuristik untuk memilih kecocokan yang “paling spesifik”. Dukungan ini sedang "
"dikembangkan dengan nama [specialization](https://rust-lang.github.io/rfcs/"
"1210-impl-specialization.html)."

#: src/generics/impl-trait.md
msgid ""
"Similar to trait bounds, an `impl Trait` syntax can be used in function "
"arguments and return values:"
msgstr ""
"Serupa dengan trait bound, sintaks `impl Trait` dapat digunakan pada argumen "
"fungsi dan nilai kembalian:"

#: src/generics/impl-trait.md
msgid ""
"// Syntactic sugar for:\n"
"//   fn add_42_millions<T: Into<i32>>(x: T) -> i32 {\n"
msgstr ""
"// Syntactic sugar for:\n"
"//   fn add_42_millions<T: Into<i32>>(x: T) -> i32 {\n"

#: src/generics/impl-trait.md
msgid ""
"`impl Trait` allows you to work with types that you cannot name. The meaning "
"of `impl Trait` is a bit different in the different positions."
msgstr ""
"`impl Trait` memungkinkan Anda menggunakan tipe yang tidak dapat disebutkan "
"namanya. Makna `impl Trait` sedikit berbeda menurut posisinya."

#: src/generics/impl-trait.md
msgid ""
"For a parameter, `impl Trait` is like an anonymous generic parameter with a "
"trait bound."
msgstr ""
"Pada parameter, `impl Trait` serupa dengan parameter generic anonim yang "
"memiliki trait bound."

#: src/generics/impl-trait.md
msgid ""
"For a return type, it means that the return type is some concrete type that "
"implements the trait, without naming the type. This can be useful when you "
"don't want to expose the concrete type in a public API."
msgstr ""
"Pada tipe nilai kembalian, bentuk ini berarti nilainya memiliki suatu tipe "
"konkret yang mengimplementasikan trait tersebut, tanpa menyebut nama tipenya. "
"Ini berguna jika Anda tidak ingin mengekspos tipe konkret dalam API publik."

#: src/generics/impl-trait.md
msgid ""
"Inference is hard in return position. A function returning `impl Foo` picks "
"the concrete type it returns, without writing it out in the source. A "
"function returning a generic type like `collect<B>() -> B` can return any "
"type satisfying `B`, and the caller may need to choose one, such as with `let "
"x: Vec<_> = foo.collect()` or with the turbofish, `foo.collect::<Vec<_>>()`."
msgstr ""
"Inference sulit dilakukan pada posisi nilai kembalian. Fungsi yang "
"mengembalikan `impl Foo` memilih sendiri tipe konkret yang dikembalikan tanpa "
"menuliskannya dalam sumber. Fungsi yang mengembalikan tipe generic, seperti "
"`collect<B>() -> B`, dapat mengembalikan tipe apa pun yang memenuhi `B`. "
"Caller mungkin perlu memilih tipenya, misalnya melalui `let x: Vec<_> = "
"foo.collect()` atau turbofish `foo.collect::<Vec<_>>()`."

#: src/generics/impl-trait.md
msgid ""
"What is the type of `debuggable`? Try `let debuggable: () = ..` to see what "
"the error message shows."
msgstr ""
"Apa tipe `debuggable`? Coba `let debuggable: () = ..` untuk melihat pesan "
"error yang muncul."

#: src/generics/dyn-trait.md
msgid ""
"In addition to using traits for static dispatch via generics, Rust also "
"supports using them for type-erased, dynamic dispatch via trait objects:"
msgstr ""
"Selain menggunakan trait untuk static dispatch melalui generics, Rust "
"mendukung dynamic dispatch dengan type erasure melalui trait object:"

#: src/generics/dyn-trait.md src/smart-pointers/trait-objects.md
msgid "\"Miau!\""
msgstr "\"Miau!\""

#: src/generics/dyn-trait.md
msgid "// Uses generics and static dispatch.\n"
msgstr "// Uses generics and static dispatch.\n"

#: src/generics/dyn-trait.md src/smart-pointers/trait-objects.md
msgid "\"Hello, who are you? {}\""
msgstr "\"Hello, who are you? {}\""

#: src/generics/dyn-trait.md
msgid "// Uses type-erasure and dynamic dispatch.\n"
msgstr "// Uses type-erasure and dynamic dispatch.\n"

#: src/generics/dyn-trait.md
msgid ""
"Generics, including `impl Trait`, use monomorphization to create a "
"specialized instance of the function for each different type that the generic "
"is instantiated with. This means that calling a trait method from within a "
"generic function still uses static dispatch, as the compiler has full type "
"information and can resolve that type's trait implementation to use."
msgstr ""
"Generics, termasuk `impl Trait`, menggunakan monomorphization untuk membuat "
"instance fungsi khusus bagi setiap tipe yang digunakan dalam instansiasi "
"generic. Artinya, pemanggilan method trait dalam fungsi generic tetap "
"menggunakan static dispatch karena compiler memiliki informasi tipe lengkap "
"dan dapat menentukan implementasi trait yang digunakan."

#: src/generics/dyn-trait.md
msgid ""
"When using `dyn Trait`, it instead uses dynamic dispatch through a [virtual "
"method table](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_method_table) (vtable). "
"This means that there's a single version of `fn dynamic` that is used "
"regardless of what type of `Pet` is passed in."
msgstr ""
"Ketika menggunakan `dyn Trait`, pemanggilan menggunakan dynamic dispatch "
"melalui [virtual method table](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Virtual_method_table) (vtable). Artinya, hanya ada satu versi `fn dynamic` "
"yang digunakan, apa pun tipe `Pet` yang diteruskan."

#: src/generics/dyn-trait.md
msgid ""
"When using `dyn Trait`, the trait object needs to be behind some kind of "
"indirection. In this case it's a reference, though smart pointer types like "
"`Box` can also be used (this will be demonstrated on day 3)."
msgstr ""
"Ketika menggunakan `dyn Trait`, trait object perlu diakses melalui suatu "
"bentuk indirection. Dalam contoh ini digunakan reference, tetapi smart "
"pointer seperti `Box` juga dapat digunakan; ini diperagakan pada hari 3."

#: src/generics/dyn-trait.md
msgid ""
"At runtime, a `&dyn Pet` is represented as a \"fat pointer\", i.e. a pair of "
"two pointers: One pointer points to the concrete object that implements "
"`Pet`, and the other points to the vtable for the trait implementation for "
"that type. When calling the `talk` method on `&dyn Pet` the compiler looks up "
"the function pointer for `talk` in the vtable and then invokes the function, "
"passing the pointer to the `Dog` or `Cat` into that function. The compiler "
"doesn't need to know the concrete type of the `Pet` in order to do this."
msgstr ""
"Saat runtime, `&dyn Pet` direpresentasikan sebagai “fat pointer”, yaitu "
"sepasang pointer. Satu pointer merujuk objek konkret yang mengimplementasikan "
"`Pet`, sedangkan yang lain merujuk vtable implementasi trait bagi tipe "
"tersebut. Saat method `talk` dipanggil pada `&dyn Pet`, compiler mencari "
"function pointer untuk `talk` dalam vtable, lalu memanggil fungsi dengan "
"meneruskan pointer ke `Dog` atau `Cat`. Compiler tidak perlu mengetahui tipe "
"konkret `Pet` untuk melakukannya."

#: src/generics/dyn-trait.md
msgid ""
"A `dyn Trait` is considered to be \"type-erased\", because we no longer have "
"compile-time knowledge of what the concrete type is."
msgstr ""
"`dyn Trait` dianggap “type-erased” karena kita tidak lagi mengetahui tipe "
"konkretnya saat compile time."

