msgstr "\"Could not read file content\""

#: src/std-types/result.md src/error-handling/result.md
msgid "\"The diary could not be opened: {err}\""
msgstr "\"The diary could not be opened: {err}\""

#: src/std-types/result.md
msgid ""
"As with `Option`, the successful value sits inside of `Result`, forcing the "
"developer to explicitly extract it. This encourages error checking. In the "
"case where an error should never happen, `unwrap()` or `expect()` can be "
"called, and this is a signal of the developer intent too."
msgstr ""
"Seperti pada `Option`, nilai hasil keberhasilan berada di dalam `Result`, "
"sehingga developer harus mengambilnya secara eksplisit. Ini mendorong "
"pemeriksaan error. Jika error seharusnya tidak pernah terjadi, `unwrap()` "
"atau `expect()` dapat dipanggil, sekaligus menunjukkan maksud developer."

#: src/std-types/result.md
msgid ""
"`Result` documentation is a recommended read. Not during the course, but it "
"is worth mentioning. It contains many convenience methods and functions that "
"help functional-style programming."
msgstr ""
"Dokumentasi `Result` disarankan untuk dibaca. Tidak perlu saat kursus, tetapi "
"layak disebutkan. Dokumentasi ini memuat banyak method dan fungsi praktis "
"yang membantu pemrograman bergaya fungsional."

#: src/std-types/result.md
msgid ""
"`Result` is the standard type to implement error handling as we will see on "
"Day 4."
msgstr ""
"`Result` merupakan tipe standar untuk mengimplementasikan error handling, "
"seperti yang akan kita lihat pada Hari 4."

