#: src/std-types/vec.md
msgid ""
"`Vec` implements [`Deref<Target = [T]>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/vec/"
"struct.Vec.html#deref-methods-%5BT%5D), which means that you can call slice "
"methods on a `Vec`."
msgstr ""
"`Vec` mengimplementasikan [`Deref<Target = [T]>`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"std/vec/struct.Vec.html#deref-methods-%5BT%5D), sehingga method slice dapat "
"dipanggil pada `Vec`."

#: src/std-types/vec.md
msgid ""
"`Vec` is a type of collection, along with `String` and `HashMap`. The data it "
"contains is stored on the heap. This means the amount of data doesn't need to "
"be known at compile time. It can grow or shrink at runtime."
msgstr ""
"`Vec` merupakan tipe collection, seperti `String` dan `HashMap`. Data di "
"dalamnya disimpan pada heap. Karena itu, jumlah data tidak perlu diketahui "
"saat compile time dan dapat bertambah atau berkurang saat runtime."

#: src/std-types/vec.md
msgid ""
"Notice how `Vec<T>` is a generic type too, but you don't have to specify `T` "
"explicitly. As always with Rust type inference, the `T` was established "
"during the first `push` call."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `Vec<T>` juga merupakan tipe generic, tetapi `T` tidak harus "
"ditulis secara eksplisit. Seperti biasa dalam type inference Rust, `T` "
"ditentukan pada pemanggilan `push` pertama."

#: src/std-types/vec.md
msgid ""
"`vec![...]` is a canonical macro to use instead of `Vec::new()` and it "
"supports adding initial elements to the vector."
msgstr ""
"`vec![...]` merupakan macro yang umum digunakan sebagai pengganti "
"`Vec::new()` dan mendukung penambahan elemen awal pada vector."

#: src/std-types/vec.md
msgid ""
"To index the vector you use `[` `]`, but they will panic if out of bounds. "
"Alternatively, using `get` will return an `Option`. The `pop` function will "
"remove the last element."
msgstr ""
"Untuk mengindeks vector, gunakan `[` `]`, tetapi akses di luar batas akan "
"memicu panic. Sebagai alternatif, `get` mengembalikan `Option`. Fungsi `pop` "
"menghapus elemen terakhir."

#: src/std-types/vec.md
msgid ""
"Students may ask why `Vec` and slices have so many inherent methods rather "
"than the standard library exposing container traits. The primary reason for "
"this design is that Rust centralizes functionality on the `Iterator` trait "
"instead, which abstracts over both I/O streams and collections, while "
"avoiding materialization of intermediate collections."
msgstr ""
"Peserta mungkin bertanya mengapa `Vec` dan slice memiliki begitu banyak "
"inherent method, alih-alih standard library menyediakan trait container. "
"Alasan utama desain ini adalah Rust memusatkan fungsionalitas pada trait "
"`Iterator`, yang mengabstraksikan I/O stream dan collection sekaligus "
"menghindari pembuatan collection perantara."

