#: src/std-traits.md
msgid ""
"As with the standard library types, spend time reviewing the documentation "
"for each trait."
msgstr ""
"Seperti pada tipe standard library, luangkan waktu untuk membaca dokumentasi "
"setiap trait."

#: src/std-traits.md
msgid "This section is long. Take a break midway through."
msgstr "Bagian ini panjang. Beristirahatlah di tengah pembahasan."

#: src/std-traits/comparisons.md
msgid ""
"These traits support comparisons between values. All traits can be derived "
"for types containing fields that implement these traits."
msgstr ""
"Trait-trait ini mendukung perbandingan nilai. Semuanya dapat di-derive untuk "
"tipe yang field-nya mengimplementasikan trait tersebut."

#: src/std-traits/comparisons.md
msgid "`PartialEq` and `Eq`"
msgstr "`PartialEq` dan `Eq`"

#: src/std-traits/comparisons.md
msgid ""
"`PartialEq` is a partial equivalence relation, with required method `eq` and "
"provided method `ne`. The `==` and `!=` operators will call these methods."
msgstr ""
"`PartialEq` merupakan partial equivalence relation, dengan method wajib `eq` "
"dan method yang disediakan `ne`. Operator `==` dan `!=` memanggil method-"
"method tersebut."

#: src/std-traits/comparisons.md
msgid ""
"`Eq` is a full equivalence relation (reflexive, symmetric, and transitive) "
"and implies `PartialEq`. Functions that require full equivalence will use "
"`Eq` as a trait bound."
msgstr ""
"`Eq` merupakan equivalence relation penuh, yaitu reflexive, symmetric, dan "
"transitive, serta mengimplikasikan `PartialEq`. Fungsi yang memerlukan "
"ekuivalensi penuh menggunakan `Eq` sebagai trait bound."

#: src/std-traits/comparisons.md
msgid "`PartialOrd` and `Ord`"
msgstr "`PartialOrd` dan `Ord`"

#: src/std-traits/comparisons.md
msgid ""
"`PartialOrd` defines a partial ordering, with a `partial_cmp` method. It is "
"used to implement the `<`, `<=`, `>=`, and `>` operators."
msgstr ""
"`PartialOrd` mendefinisikan partial ordering melalui method `partial_cmp`. "
"Trait ini digunakan untuk mengimplementasikan operator `<`, `<=`, `>=`, dan "
"`>`."

#: src/std-traits/comparisons.md
msgid "`Ord` is a total ordering, with `cmp` returning `Ordering`."
msgstr ""
"`Ord` merupakan total ordering, dengan `cmp` yang mengembalikan `Ordering`."

#: src/std-traits/comparisons.md
msgid ""
"`PartialEq` can be implemented between different types, but `Eq` cannot, "
"because it is reflexive:"
msgstr ""
"`PartialEq` dapat diimplementasikan antara tipe berbeda, tetapi `Eq` tidak, "
"karena bersifat reflexive:"

#: src/std-traits/comparisons.md
msgid ""
"In practice, it's common to derive these traits, but uncommon to implement "
"them."
msgstr ""
"Dalam praktiknya, deriving trait-trait ini umum dilakukan, tetapi "
"implementasi manualnya jarang."

#: src/std-traits/comparisons.md
msgid ""
"When comparing references in Rust, it will compare the value of the things "
"pointed to, it will NOT compare the references themselves. That means that "
"references to two different things can compare as equal if the values pointed "
"to are the same:"
msgstr ""
"Saat membandingkan reference, Rust membandingkan nilai yang dirujuk, BUKAN "
"reference itu sendiri. Artinya, reference ke dua objek berbeda dapat dianggap "
"sama jika nilai yang dirujuk sama:"

#: src/std-traits/operators.md
msgid ""
"Operator overloading is implemented via traits in [`std::ops`](https://"
"doc.rust-lang.org/std/ops/index.html):"
msgstr ""
"Operator overloading diimplementasikan melalui trait dalam [`std::ops`]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ops/index.html):"

#: src/std-traits/operators.md
msgid "\"{p1:?} + {p2:?} = {:?}\""
msgstr "\"{p1:?} + {p2:?} = {:?}\""

#: src/std-traits/operators.md src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid "Discussion points:"
msgstr "Bahan diskusi:"

#: src/std-traits/operators.md
msgid ""
"You could implement `Add` for `&Point`. In which situations is that useful?"
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat mengimplementasikan `Add` untuk `&Point`. Dalam situasi apa ini "
"berguna?"

#: src/std-traits/operators.md
msgid ""
"Answer: `Add::add` consumes `self`. If type `T` for which you are overloading "
"the operator is not `Copy`, you should consider overloading the operator for "
"`&T` as well. This avoids unnecessary cloning on the call site."
msgstr ""
"Jawaban: `Add::add` mengonsumsi `self`. Jika tipe `T` yang operatornya Anda "
"overload tidak bersifat `Copy`, pertimbangkan juga overloading operator untuk "
"`&T`. Ini menghindari cloning yang tidak diperlukan di tempat pemanggilan."

#: src/std-traits/operators.md
msgid ""
"Why is `Output` an associated type? Could it be made a type parameter of the "
"method?"
msgstr ""
"Mengapa `Output` merupakan associated type? Dapatkah bentuk ini dijadikan "
"parameter tipe method?"

#: src/std-traits/operators.md
msgid ""
"Short answer: Function type parameters are controlled by the caller, but "
"associated types (like `Output`) are controlled by the implementer of a trait."
msgstr ""
"Jawaban singkat: parameter tipe fungsi ditentukan caller, sedangkan "
"associated type, seperti `Output`, ditentukan implementer trait."

#: src/std-traits/operators.md
msgid ""
"You could implement `Add` for two different types, e.g. `impl Add<(i32, i32)> "
"for Point` would add a tuple to a `Point`."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat mengimplementasikan `Add` untuk dua tipe berbeda. Misalnya, `impl "
"Add<(i32, i32)> for Point` menambahkan tuple ke `Point`."

#: src/std-traits/operators.md
msgid ""
"The `Not` trait (`!` operator) is notable because it does not convert the "
"argument to `bool` like the same operator in C-family languages; instead, for "
"integer types it flips each bit of the number, which, arithmetically, is "
"equivalent to subtracting the argument from `-1`: `!5 == -6`."
msgstr ""
"Trait `Not`, yaitu operator `!`, menarik karena tidak mengonversi argumen "
"menjadi `bool` seperti operator serupa dalam keluarga bahasa C. Untuk tipe "
"integer, operator ini membalik setiap bit angka, yang secara aritmetika "
"setara dengan mengurangkan argumen dari `-1`: `!5 == -6`."

#: src/std-traits/from-and-into.md
msgid ""
"Types implement [`From`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/"
"trait.From.html) and [`Into`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/"
"trait.Into.html) to facilitate type conversions. Unlike `as`, these traits "
"correspond to lossless, infallible conversions."
msgstr ""
"Tipe mengimplementasikan [`From`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/"
"trait.From.html) dan [`Into`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/"
"trait.Into.html) untuk memudahkan konversi tipe. Berbeda dari `as`, trait-"
"trait ini digunakan untuk konversi yang lossless dan infallible."

#: src/std-traits/from-and-into.md
msgid "\"{s}, {addr}, {one}, {bigger}\""
msgstr "\"{s}, {addr}, {one}, {bigger}\""

#: src/std-traits/from-and-into.md
msgid ""
"[`Into`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/trait.Into.html) is "
"automatically implemented when [`From`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/"
"trait.From.html) is implemented:"
msgstr ""
"[`Into`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/trait.Into.html) otomatis "
"diimplementasikan ketika [`From`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/convert/"
"trait.From.html) diimplementasikan:"

#: src/std-traits/from-and-into.md
msgid ""
"That's why it is common to only implement `From`, as your type will get "
"`Into` implementation too."
msgstr ""
"Karena itu, biasanya cukup mengimplementasikan `From`, sebab tipe Anda juga "
"mendapatkan implementasi `Into`."

#: src/std-traits/from-and-into.md
msgid ""
"When declaring a function argument input type like \"anything that can be "
"converted into a `String`\", the rule is opposite, you should use `Into`. "
"Your function will accept types that implement `From` and those that _only_ "
"implement `Into`."
msgstr ""
"Saat mendeklarasikan tipe argumen fungsi seperti “apa pun yang dapat "
"dikonversi menjadi `String`”, aturannya berkebalikan: sebaiknya gunakan "
"`Into`. Fungsi Anda akan menerima tipe yang mengimplementasikan `From` maupun "
"yang _hanya_ mengimplementasikan `Into`."

#: src/std-traits/casting.md
msgid ""
"Rust has no _implicit_ type conversions, but does support explicit casts with "
"`as`. These generally follow C semantics where those are defined."
msgstr ""
"Rust tidak memiliki konversi tipe _implisit_, tetapi mendukung cast eksplisit "
"menggunakan `as`. Secara umum, cast ini mengikuti semantik C jika perilakunya "
"memang ditentukan di sana."

#: src/std-traits/casting.md
msgid "\"as u16: {}\""
msgstr "\"as u16: {}\""

#: src/std-traits/casting.md
msgid "\"as i16: {}\""
msgstr "\"as i16: {}\""

#: src/std-traits/casting.md
msgid "\"as u8: {}\""
msgstr "\"as u8: {}\""

#: src/std-traits/casting.md
msgid ""
"The results of `as` are _always_ defined in Rust and consistent across "
"platforms. This might not match your intuition for changing sign or casting "
"to a smaller type -- check the docs, and comment for clarity."
msgstr ""
"Hasil `as` _selalu_ memiliki perilaku yang ditentukan dalam Rust dan "
"konsisten antarplatform. Hasilnya mungkin tidak sesuai intuisi Anda saat "
"mengubah tanda atau melakukan cast ke tipe lebih kecil. Periksa dokumentasi "
"dan tambahkan komentar agar jelas."

#: src/std-traits/casting.md
msgid ""
"Casting with `as` is a relatively sharp tool that is easy to use incorrectly, "
"and can be a source of subtle bugs as future maintenance work changes the "
"types that are used or the ranges of values in types. Casts are best used "
"only when the intent is to indicate unconditional truncation (e.g. selecting "
"the bottom 32 bits of a `u64` with `as u32`, regardless of what was in the "
"high bits)."
msgstr ""
"Casting dengan `as` merupakan alat yang cukup tajam dan mudah disalahgunakan. "
"Ini dapat menimbulkan bug halus ketika pemeliharaan berikutnya mengubah tipe "
"atau rentang nilainya. Cast sebaiknya hanya digunakan ketika memang "
"dimaksudkan untuk truncation tanpa syarat, misalnya mengambil 32 bit terbawah "
"dari `u64` menggunakan `as u32`, apa pun isi bit atasnya."

#: src/std-traits/casting.md
msgid ""
"For infallible casts (e.g. `u32` to `u64`), prefer using `From` or `Into` "
"over `as` to confirm that the cast is in fact infallible. For fallible casts, "
"`TryFrom` and `TryInto` are available when you want to handle casts that fit "
"differently from those that don't."
msgstr ""
"Untuk cast infallible, misalnya `u32` ke `u64`, utamakan `From` atau `Into` "
"daripada `as` agar dipastikan bahwa konversinya memang infallible. Untuk cast "
"fallible, tersedia `TryFrom` dan `TryInto` ketika Anda ingin membedakan "
"penanganan nilai yang muat dan tidak muat pada tipe tujuan."

#: src/std-traits/casting.md
msgid "Consider taking a break after this slide."
msgstr "Pertimbangkan beristirahat setelah slide ini."

#: src/std-traits/casting.md
msgid ""
"`as` is similar to a C++ static cast. Use of `as` in cases where data might "
"be lost is generally discouraged, or at least deserves an explanatory comment."
msgstr ""
"`as` serupa dengan static cast C++. Penggunaan `as` ketika ada kemungkinan "
"kehilangan data umumnya tidak disarankan, atau setidaknya perlu disertai "
"komentar penjelas."

#: src/std-traits/casting.md
msgid "This is common in casting integers to `usize` for use as an index."
msgstr ""
"Ini umum terjadi ketika integer di-cast menjadi `usize` untuk digunakan "
"sebagai indeks."

#: src/std-traits/read-and-write.md
msgid ""
"Using [`Read`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/trait.Read.html) and "
"[`BufRead`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/trait.BufRead.html), you can "
"abstract over `u8` sources:"
msgstr ""
"Dengan [`Read`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/trait.Read.html) dan "
"[`BufRead`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/trait.BufRead.html), Anda dapat "
"mengabstraksikan sumber `u8`:"

#: src/std-traits/read-and-write.md
msgid "b\"foo\\nbar\\nbaz\\n\""
msgstr "b\"foo\\nbar\\nbaz\\n\""

#: src/std-traits/read-and-write.md
msgid "\"lines in slice: {}\""
msgstr "\"lines in slice: {}\""

#: src/std-traits/read-and-write.md
msgid "\"lines in file: {}\""
msgstr "\"lines in file: {}\""

#: src/std-traits/read-and-write.md
msgid ""
"Similarly, [`Write`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/trait.Write.html) lets "
"you abstract over `u8` sinks:"
msgstr ""
"Demikian pula, [`Write`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/io/trait.Write.html) "
"memungkinkan abstraksi atas tujuan penulisan `u8`:"

#: src/std-traits/read-and-write.md
msgid "\"\\n\""
msgstr "\"\\n\""

#: src/std-traits/read-and-write.md
