msgstr "\"Logged: {buffer:?}\""

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid "The `Default` Trait"
msgstr "Trait `Default`"

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid ""
"The [`Default`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/default/trait.Default.html) "
"trait produces a default value for a type."
msgstr ""
"Trait [`Default`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/default/trait.Default.html) "
"menghasilkan nilai default bagi suatu tipe."

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid "\"John Smith\""
msgstr "\"John Smith\""

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid "\"Y is set!\""
msgstr "\"Y is set!\""

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid ""
"It can be implemented directly or it can be derived via `#[derive(Default)]`."
msgstr ""
"Trait ini dapat diimplementasikan langsung atau di-derive melalui "
"`#[derive(Default)]`."

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid ""
"A derived implementation will produce a value where all fields are set to "
"their default values."
msgstr ""
"Implementasi hasil derive menghasilkan nilai dengan semua field diatur ke "
"nilai default masing-masing."

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid "This means all types in the struct must implement `Default` too."
msgstr ""
"Artinya, semua tipe dalam struct juga harus mengimplementasikan `Default`."

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid ""
"Standard Rust types commonly implement `Default` with reasonable values (e.g. "
"`0`, `\"\"`, etc)."
msgstr ""
"Tipe standar Rust umumnya mengimplementasikan `Default` dengan nilai yang "
"wajar, misalnya `0`, `\"\"`, dan sebagainya."

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid "The partial struct initialization works nicely with default."
msgstr "Inisialisasi struct secara parsial cocok digunakan bersama default."

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid ""
"The Rust standard library is aware that types can implement `Default` and "
"provides convenience methods that use it."
msgstr ""
"Standard library Rust memperhitungkan bahwa tipe dapat mengimplementasikan "
"`Default` dan menyediakan method praktis yang memanfaatkannya."

#: src/std-traits/default.md
msgid ""
"The `..` syntax is called [struct update syntax](https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"book/ch05-01-defining-structs.html#creating-instances-from-other-instances-"
"with-struct-update-syntax)."
msgstr ""
"Sintaks `..` disebut [struct update syntax](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/"
"ch05-01-defining-structs.html#creating-instances-from-other-instances-with-"
"struct-update-syntax)."

#: src/std-traits/exercise.md
