#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Traditionally, languages have fallen into two broad categories:"
msgstr ""
"Secara tradisional, bahasa pemrograman terbagi menjadi dua kategori besar:"

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Full control via manual memory management: C, C++, Pascal, ..."
msgstr "Kendali penuh melalui pengelolaan memori manual: C, C++, Pascal, ..."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Programmer decides when to allocate or free heap memory."
msgstr "Programmer menentukan kapan memori heap dialokasikan atau dibebaskan."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"Programmer must determine whether a pointer still points to valid memory."
msgstr ""
"Programmer harus menentukan apakah pointer masih merujuk memori yang valid."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Studies show, programmers make mistakes."
msgstr "Penelitian menunjukkan bahwa programmer melakukan kesalahan."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"Full safety via automatic memory management at runtime: Java, Python, Go, "
"Haskell, ..."
msgstr ""
"Keamanan penuh melalui pengelolaan memori otomatis saat runtime: Java, "
"Python, Go, Haskell, ..."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"A runtime system ensures that memory is not freed until it can no longer be "
"referenced."
msgstr ""
"Sistem runtime memastikan memori tidak dibebaskan sampai tidak dapat dirujuk "
"lagi."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Typically implemented with reference counting or garbage collection."
msgstr ""
"Biasanya diimplementasikan menggunakan reference counting atau garbage "
"collection."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "Rust offers a new mix:"
msgstr "Rust menawarkan kombinasi baru:"

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"Full control _and_ safety via compile time enforcement of correct memory "
"management."
msgstr ""
"Kendali penuh _dan_ keamanan melalui penegakan pengelolaan memori yang benar "
"saat compile time."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid "It does this with an explicit ownership concept."
msgstr "Rust melakukannya melalui konsep ownership yang eksplisit."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"This slide is intended to help students coming from other languages to put "
"Rust in context."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini membantu peserta yang terbiasa dengan bahasa lain memahami posisi "
"Rust."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"C must manage heap manually with `malloc` and `free`. Common errors include "
"forgetting to call `free`, calling it multiple times for the same pointer, or "
"dereferencing a pointer after the memory it points to has been freed."
msgstr ""
"Dalam C, heap harus dikelola secara manual menggunakan `malloc` dan `free`. "
"Kesalahan umum meliputi lupa memanggil `free`, memanggilnya beberapa kali "
"untuk pointer yang sama, atau melakukan dereference setelah memori yang "
"dirujuk dibebaskan."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"C++ has tools like smart pointers (`unique_ptr`, `shared_ptr`) that take "
"advantage of language guarantees about calling destructors to ensure memory "
"is freed when a function returns. It is still quite easy to misuse these "
"tools and create similar bugs to C."
msgstr ""
"C++ memiliki fasilitas seperti smart pointer (`unique_ptr`, `shared_ptr`) "
"yang memanfaatkan jaminan bahasa tentang pemanggilan destructor agar memori "
"dibebaskan saat fungsi selesai. Fasilitas ini masih cukup mudah "
"disalahgunakan sehingga menimbulkan bug serupa dengan C."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"Java, Go, and Python rely on the garbage collector to identify memory that is "
"no longer reachable and discard it. This guarantees that any pointer can be "
"dereferenced, eliminating use-after-free and other classes of bugs. But, GC "
"has a runtime cost and is difficult to tune properly."
msgstr ""
"Java, Go, dan Python mengandalkan garbage collector untuk mengidentifikasi "
"dan membuang memori yang tidak lagi dapat dijangkau. Ini menjamin setiap "
"pointer dapat di-dereference, sehingga menghilangkan use-after-free dan "
"kategori bug lainnya. Namun, GC memiliki biaya runtime dan sulit disetel "
"dengan tepat."

#: src/memory-management/approaches.md
msgid ""
"Rust's ownership and borrowing model can, in many cases, get the performance "
"of C, with alloc and free operations precisely where they are required -- "
"zero-cost. It also provides tools similar to C++'s smart pointers. When "
"required, other options such as reference counting are available, and there "
"are even crates available to support runtime garbage collection (not covered "
"in this class)."
msgstr ""
"Dalam banyak kasus, model ownership dan borrowing Rust dapat mencapai "
"performa C, dengan operasi alloc dan free tepat di tempat yang diperlukan—"
"zero-cost. Rust juga menyediakan fasilitas serupa smart pointer C++. Jika "
"diperlukan, tersedia pilihan lain seperti reference counting, bahkan crate "
"yang mendukung garbage collection saat runtime, yang tidak dibahas dalam "
"kelas ini."

#: src/memory-management/ownership.md
msgid ""
"All variable bindings have a _scope_ where they are valid and it is an error "
"to use a variable outside its scope:"
msgstr ""
"Semua variable binding memiliki _scope_ tempat binding tersebut valid. "
"Menggunakan variabel di luar scope merupakan error:"

#: src/memory-management/ownership.md
msgid ""
"We say that the variable _owns_ the value. Every Rust value has precisely one "
"owner at all times."
msgstr ""
"Kita menyebut variabel sebagai _pemilik_ nilai. Setiap nilai Rust selalu "
"memiliki tepat satu owner."

#: src/memory-management/ownership.md
msgid ""
"At the end of the scope, the variable is _dropped_ and the data is freed. A "
"destructor can run here to free up resources."
msgstr ""
"Pada akhir scope, variabel _di-drop_ dan datanya dibebaskan. Destructor dapat "
"dijalankan di sini untuk membebaskan resource."

#: src/memory-management/ownership.md
msgid ""
"Students familiar with garbage collection implementations will know that a "
"garbage collector starts with a set of \"roots\" to find all reachable "
"memory. Rust's \"single owner\" principle is a similar idea."
msgstr ""
"Peserta yang mengenal implementasi garbage collection mengetahui bahwa "
"garbage collector berawal dari sekumpulan “root” untuk menemukan semua memori "
"yang dapat dijangkau. Prinsip “single owner” Rust merupakan gagasan serupa."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "An assignment will transfer _ownership_ between variables:"
msgstr "Assignment memindahkan _ownership_ antarvariabel:"

#: src/memory-management/move.md src/concurrency/async-control-flow/select.md
