msgstr "// say_hello(name);\n"

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"Mention that this is the opposite of the defaults in C++, which copies by "
"value unless you use `std::move` (and the move constructor is defined!)."
msgstr ""
"Sampaikan bahwa ini berkebalikan dengan perilaku default C++, yang menyalin "
"by value kecuali Anda menggunakan `std::move` dan move constructor telah "
"didefinisikan!"

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"It is only the ownership that moves. Whether any machine code is generated to "
"manipulate the data itself is a matter of optimization, and such copies are "
"aggressively optimized away."
msgstr ""
"Hanya ownership yang berpindah. Ada atau tidaknya machine code untuk "
"memanipulasi data bergantung pada optimasi, dan penyalinan semacam itu "
"dihilangkan secara agresif melalui optimasi."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"Simple values (such as integers) can be marked `Copy` (see later slides)."
msgstr ""
"Nilai sederhana, seperti integer, dapat ditandai `Copy`; lihat slide "
"selanjutnya."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "In Rust, clones are explicit (by using `clone`)."
msgstr "Dalam Rust, cloning dilakukan secara eksplisit menggunakan `clone`."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "In the `say_hello` example:"
msgstr "Dalam contoh `say_hello`:"

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"With the first call to `say_hello`, `main` gives up ownership of `name`. "
"Afterwards, `name` cannot be used anymore within `main`."
msgstr ""
"Pada pemanggilan pertama `say_hello`, `main` menyerahkan ownership atas "
"`name`. Setelahnya, `name` tidak dapat digunakan lagi dalam `main`."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"The heap memory allocated for `name` will be freed at the end of the "
"`say_hello` function."
msgstr ""
"Memori heap yang dialokasikan untuk `name` dibebaskan pada akhir fungsi "
"`say_hello`."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"`main` can retain ownership if it passes `name` as a reference (`&name`) and "
"if `say_hello` accepts a reference as a parameter."
msgstr ""
"`main` dapat mempertahankan ownership jika meneruskan `name` sebagai "
"reference (`&name`) dan `say_hello` menerima reference sebagai parameter."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"Alternatively, `main` can pass a clone of `name` in the first call "
"(`name.clone()`)."
msgstr ""
"Sebagai alternatif, `main` dapat meneruskan hasil clone `name` pada "
"pemanggilan pertama (`name.clone()`)."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"Rust makes it harder than C++ to inadvertently create copies by making move "
"semantics the default, and by forcing programmers to make clones explicit."
msgstr ""
"Rust mempersulit penyalinan yang tidak disengaja dibandingkan C++, dengan "
"menjadikan move semantics sebagai perilaku default dan mengharuskan cloning "
"dilakukan secara eksplisit."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "Defensive Copies in Modern C++"
msgstr "Defensive Copy dalam C++ Modern"

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "Modern C++ solves this differently:"
msgstr "C++ modern mengatasinya dengan cara berbeda:"

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "\"Cpp\""
msgstr "\"Cpp\""

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "// Duplicate the data in s1.\n"
msgstr "// Duplicate the data in s1.\n"

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"The heap data from `s1` is duplicated and `s2` gets its own independent copy."
msgstr ""
"Data heap milik `s1` diduplikasi, dan `s2` mendapatkan salinan tersendiri "
"yang terpisah."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "When `s1` and `s2` go out of scope, they each free their own memory."
msgstr ""
"Ketika `s1` dan `s2` keluar dari scope, masing-masing membebaskan memorinya "
"sendiri."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "Before copy-assignment:"
msgstr "Sebelum copy-assignment:"

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid "After copy-assignment:"
msgstr "Setelah copy-assignment:"

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"C++ has made a slightly different choice than Rust. Because `=` copies data, "
"the string data has to be cloned. Otherwise we would get a double-free when "
"either string goes out of scope."
msgstr ""
"C++ mengambil pilihan yang sedikit berbeda dari Rust. Karena `=` menyalin "
"data, data string harus di-clone. Jika tidak, double-free akan terjadi ketika "
"salah satu string keluar dari scope."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"C++ also has [`std::move`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/move), "
"which is used to indicate when a value may be moved from. If the example had "
"been `s2 = std::move(s1)`, no heap allocation would take place. After the "
"move, `s1` would be in a valid but unspecified state. Unlike Rust, the "
"programmer is allowed to keep using `s1`."
msgstr ""
"C++ juga memiliki [`std::move`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/"
"move), yang menandai bahwa nilai boleh dipindahkan darinya. Jika contoh "
"menggunakan `s2 = std::move(s1)`, tidak ada alokasi heap. Setelah move, `s1` "
"berada dalam state yang valid tetapi tidak ditentukan. Berbeda dari Rust, "
"programmer tetap boleh menggunakan `s1`."

#: src/memory-management/move.md
msgid ""
"Unlike Rust, `=` in C++ can run arbitrary code as determined by the type that "
"is being copied or moved."
msgstr ""
"Berbeda dari Rust, `=` dalam C++ dapat menjalankan kode apa pun sesuai "
"ketentuan tipe yang disalin atau dipindahkan."

#: src/memory-management/clone.md
msgid ""
"Sometimes you _want_ to make a copy of a value. The `Clone` trait "
"accomplishes this."
msgstr ""
"Terkadang Anda memang _ingin_ menyalin suatu nilai. Trait `Clone` menyediakan "
"kemampuan ini."

#: src/memory-management/clone.md
msgid ""
"The idea of `Clone` is to make it easy to spot where heap allocations are "
"occurring. Look for `.clone()` and a few others like `vec!` or `Box::new`."
msgstr ""
"Gagasan `Clone` adalah memudahkan penemuan tempat alokasi heap terjadi. Cari "
"`.clone()` dan beberapa bentuk lain seperti `vec!` atau `Box::new`."

#: src/memory-management/clone.md
msgid ""
"It's common to \"clone your way out\" of problems with the borrow checker, "
"and return later to try to optimize those clones away."
msgstr ""
"Mengatasi masalah borrow checker dengan cloning terlebih dahulu merupakan hal "
"yang umum, lalu kembali nanti untuk mencoba menghilangkan cloning tersebut "
"melalui optimasi."

#: src/memory-management/clone.md
msgid ""
"`clone` generally performs a deep copy of the value, meaning that if you e.g. "
"clone an array, all of the elements of the array are cloned as well."
msgstr ""
"`clone` umumnya melakukan deep copy nilai. Misalnya, ketika meng-clone array, "
"semua elemennya juga di-clone."

#: src/memory-management/clone.md
msgid ""
"The behavior for `clone` is user-defined, so it can perform custom cloning "
"logic if needed."
msgstr ""
"Perilaku `clone` ditentukan pengguna, sehingga dapat menjalankan logika "
"cloning khusus jika diperlukan."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid ""
"While move semantics are the default, certain types are copied by default:"
msgstr ""
"Walaupun move semantics merupakan perilaku default, tipe tertentu secara "
"default disalin:"

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid "These types implement the `Copy` trait."
msgstr "Tipe-tipe ini mengimplementasikan trait `Copy`."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid "You can opt-in your own types to use copy semantics:"
msgstr "Anda dapat memilih agar tipe buatan sendiri menggunakan copy semantics:"

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid "After the assignment, both `p1` and `p2` own their own data."
msgstr ""
"Setelah assignment, `p1` dan `p2` masing-masing memiliki datanya sendiri."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid "We can also use `p1.clone()` to explicitly copy the data."
msgstr ""
"Kita juga dapat menggunakan `p1.clone()` untuk menyalin data secara eksplisit."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid "Copying and cloning are not the same thing:"
msgstr "Copying dan cloning merupakan dua hal berbeda:"

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid ""
"Copying refers to bitwise copies of memory regions and does not work on "
"arbitrary objects."
msgstr ""
"Copying merujuk penyalinan bitwise pada area memori dan tidak dapat "
"diterapkan pada sembarang objek."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid ""
"Copying does not allow for custom logic (unlike copy constructors in C++)."
msgstr ""
"Copying tidak mengizinkan logika khusus, berbeda dari copy constructor dalam "
"C++."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid ""
"Cloning is a more general operation and also allows for custom behavior by "
"implementing the `Clone` trait."
msgstr ""
"Cloning merupakan operasi yang lebih umum dan memungkinkan perilaku khusus "
"melalui implementasi trait `Clone`."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid "Copying does not work on types that implement the `Drop` trait."
msgstr ""
"Copying tidak dapat diterapkan pada tipe yang mengimplementasikan trait "
"`Drop`."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid "In the above example, try the following:"
msgstr "Pada contoh di atas, coba langkah berikut:"

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid ""
"Add a `String` field to `struct Point`. It will not compile because `String` "
"is not a `Copy` type."
msgstr ""
"Tambahkan field `String` pada `struct Point`. Kode tidak dapat dikompilasi "
"karena `String` bukan tipe `Copy`."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid ""
"Remove `Copy` from the `derive` attribute. The compiler error is now in the "
"`println!` for `p1`."
msgstr ""
"Hapus `Copy` dari atribut `derive`. Kini error compiler muncul pada `println!"
"` untuk `p1`."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid "Show that it works if you clone `p1` instead."
msgstr "Tunjukkan bahwa kode bekerja jika Anda meng-clone `p1`."

#: src/memory-management/copy-types.md
msgid ""
"Shared references are `Copy`/`Clone`, mutable references are not. This is "
"because Rust requires that mutable references be exclusive, so while it's "
"valid to make a copy of a shared reference, creating a copy of a mutable "
"reference would violate Rust's borrowing rules."
msgstr ""
"Shared reference bersifat `Copy`/`Clone`, sedangkan mutable reference tidak. "
"Rust mengharuskan mutable reference bersifat eksklusif. Karena itu, menyalin "
"shared reference valid, tetapi menyalin mutable reference melanggar aturan "
"borrowing Rust."

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid "The `Drop` Trait"
msgstr "Trait `Drop`"

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid ""
"Values which implement [`Drop`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ops/"
"trait.Drop.html) can specify code to run when they go out of scope:"
msgstr ""
"Nilai yang mengimplementasikan [`Drop`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/ops/"
"trait.Drop.html) dapat menentukan kode yang dijalankan ketika keluar dari "
"scope:"

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
