msgid "\"c\""
msgstr "\"c\""

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid "\"d\""
msgstr "\"d\""

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid "\"Exiting innermost block\""
msgstr "\"Exiting innermost block\""

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid "\"Exiting next block\""
msgstr "\"Exiting next block\""

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid "\"Exiting main\""
msgstr "\"Exiting main\""

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid "Note that `std::mem::drop` is not the same as `std::ops::Drop::drop`."
msgstr "Perhatikan bahwa `std::mem::drop` berbeda dari `std::ops::Drop::drop`."

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid "Values are automatically dropped when they go out of scope."
msgstr "Nilai otomatis di-drop ketika keluar dari scope."

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid ""
"When a value is dropped, if it implements `std::ops::Drop` then its "
"`Drop::drop` implementation will be called."
msgstr ""
"Ketika nilai di-drop, jika mengimplementasikan `std::ops::Drop`, implementasi "
"`Drop::drop` miliknya akan dipanggil."

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid ""
"All its fields will then be dropped too, whether or not it implements `Drop`."
msgstr ""
"Semua field-nya kemudian juga di-drop, terlepas dari apakah nilai itu "
"mengimplementasikan `Drop`."

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid ""
"`std::mem::drop` is just an empty function that takes any value. The "
"significance is that it takes ownership of the value, so at the end of its "
"scope it gets dropped. This makes it a convenient way to explicitly drop "
"values earlier than they would otherwise go out of scope."
msgstr ""
"`std::mem::drop` hanyalah fungsi kosong yang menerima nilai apa pun. Hal "
"pentingnya, fungsi ini mengambil ownership nilai, sehingga nilai di-drop pada "
"akhir scope-nya. Karena itu, fungsi ini praktis untuk secara eksplisit "
"melakukan drop lebih awal, sebelum nilai tersebut keluar dari scope semula."

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid ""
"This is useful for objects that do some work on `drop`: releasing locks, "
"closing files, etc."
msgstr ""
"Ini berguna untuk objek yang melakukan pekerjaan saat `drop`, seperti melepas "
"lock, menutup berkas, dan sebagainya."

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid "Why doesn't `Drop::drop` take `self`?"
msgstr "Mengapa `Drop::drop` tidak menerima `self`?"

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid ""
"Short-answer: If it did, `std::mem::drop` would be called at the end of the "
"block, resulting in another call to `Drop::drop`, and a stack overflow!"
msgstr ""
"Jawaban singkat: jika demikian, `std::mem::drop` dipanggil pada akhir block, "
"sehingga memanggil `Drop::drop` lagi dan menyebabkan stack overflow!"

#: src/memory-management/drop.md
msgid "Try replacing `drop(a)` with `a.drop()`."
msgstr "Coba ganti `drop(a)` dengan `a.drop()`."

#: src/memory-management/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this example, we will implement a complex data type that owns all of its "
"data. We will use the \"builder pattern\" to support building a new value "
