#: src/smart-pointers/box.md
msgid ""
"`Box` is like `std::unique_ptr` in C++, except that it's guaranteed to be not "
"null."
msgstr ""
"`Box` serupa dengan `std::unique_ptr` dalam C++, tetapi dijamin tidak null."

#: src/smart-pointers/box.md
msgid "A `Box` can be useful when you:"
msgstr "`Box` dapat berguna ketika Anda:"

#: src/smart-pointers/box.md
msgid ""
"have a type whose size can't be known at compile time, but the Rust compiler "
"wants to know an exact size."
msgstr ""
"memiliki tipe yang ukurannya tidak dapat diketahui saat compile time, tetapi "
"compiler Rust memerlukan ukuran yang pasti."

#: src/smart-pointers/box.md
msgid ""
"want to transfer ownership of a large amount of data. To avoid copying large "
"amounts of data on the stack, instead store the data on the heap in a `Box` "
"so only the pointer is moved."
msgstr ""
"ingin memindahkan ownership data berukuran besar. Agar tidak menyalin banyak "
"data pada stack, simpan data pada heap dalam `Box`, sehingga hanya pointernya "
"yang dipindahkan."

#: src/smart-pointers/box.md
msgid ""
"If `Box` was not used and we attempted to embed a `List` directly into the "
"`List`, the compiler would not be able to compute a fixed size for the struct "
"in memory (the `List` would be of infinite size)."
msgstr ""
"Tanpa `Box`, jika kita mencoba menyimpan `List` langsung di dalam `List`, "
"compiler tidak dapat menghitung ukuran tetap struct dalam memori karena "
"ukuran `List` menjadi tak terhingga."

#: src/smart-pointers/box.md
msgid ""
"`Box` solves this problem as it has the same size as a regular pointer and "
"just points at the next element of the `List` in the heap."
msgstr ""
"`Box` mengatasi masalah ini karena berukuran sama dengan pointer biasa dan "
"hanya merujuk elemen `List` berikutnya pada heap."

#: src/smart-pointers/box.md
msgid ""
"Remove the `Box` in the List definition and show the compiler error. We get "
"the message \"recursive without indirection\", because for data recursion, we "
"have to use indirection, a `Box` or reference of some kind, instead of "
"storing the value directly."
msgstr ""
"Hapus `Box` pada definisi List dan tampilkan error compiler. Pesan “recursive "
"without indirection” muncul karena data rekursif harus menggunakan "
"indirection, melalui `Box` atau suatu reference, bukan menyimpan nilainya "
"langsung."

#: src/smart-pointers/box.md
msgid ""
"Though `Box` looks like `std::unique_ptr` in C++, it cannot be empty/null. "
"This makes `Box` one of the types that allow the compiler to optimize storage "
"of some enums (the \"niche optimization\")."
msgstr ""
"Walaupun `Box` serupa dengan `std::unique_ptr` dalam C++, nilainya tidak "
"dapat kosong/null. Karena itu, `Box` merupakan salah satu tipe yang "
"memungkinkan compiler mengoptimalkan penyimpanan sebagian enum melalui “niche "
"optimization”."

#: src/smart-pointers/rc.md
msgid ""
"[`Rc`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/rc/struct.Rc.html) is a reference-"
"counted shared pointer. Use this when you need to refer to the same data from "
"multiple places:"
msgstr ""
"[`Rc`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/rc/struct.Rc.html) merupakan shared "
"pointer dengan reference counting. Gunakan ketika data yang sama perlu "
"dirujuk dari beberapa tempat:"

#: src/smart-pointers/rc.md
msgid ""
"Each `Rc` points to the same shared data structure, containing strong and "
"weak pointers and the value:"
msgstr ""
"Setiap `Rc` merujuk struktur data bersama yang sama, yang memuat strong "
"pointer, weak pointer, dan nilainya:"

#: src/smart-pointers/rc.md
msgid ""
"See [`Arc`](../concurrency/shared-state/arc.md) and [`Mutex`](https://"
"doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html) if you are in a multi-threaded "
"context."
msgstr ""
"Lihat [`Arc`](../concurrency/shared-state/arc.md) dan [`Mutex`](https://"
"doc.rust-lang.org/std/sync/struct.Mutex.html) untuk konteks multithread."

#: src/smart-pointers/rc.md
msgid ""
"You can _downgrade_ a shared pointer into a [`Weak`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/std/rc/struct.Weak.html) pointer to create cycles that will get "
"dropped."
msgstr ""
"Anda dapat melakukan _downgrade_ shared pointer menjadi pointer [`Weak`]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/rc/struct.Weak.html) untuk membuat siklus yang "
"tetap dapat di-drop."

#: src/smart-pointers/rc.md
msgid ""
"`Rc`'s count ensures that its contained value is valid for as long as there "
"are references."
msgstr ""
"Hitungan pada `Rc` memastikan nilai di dalamnya tetap valid selama masih ada "
"reference."

#: src/smart-pointers/rc.md
msgid "`Rc` in Rust is like `std::shared_ptr` in C++."
msgstr "`Rc` dalam Rust serupa dengan `std::shared_ptr` dalam C++."

#: src/smart-pointers/rc.md
msgid ""
"`Rc::clone` is cheap: it creates a pointer to the same allocation and "
"increases the reference count. Does not make a deep clone and can generally "
"be ignored when looking for performance issues in code."
msgstr ""
"`Rc::clone` berbiaya rendah: membuat pointer ke alokasi yang sama dan "
"menambah reference count. Operasi ini tidak melakukan deep clone dan umumnya "
"dapat diabaikan saat mencari masalah performa kode."

#: src/smart-pointers/rc.md
msgid ""
"`make_mut` actually clones the inner value if necessary (\"clone-on-write\") "
"and returns a mutable reference."
msgstr ""
"`make_mut` benar-benar meng-clone nilai di dalamnya jika diperlukan, yaitu "
"“clone-on-write”, dan mengembalikan mutable reference."

#: src/smart-pointers/rc.md
msgid "Use `Rc::strong_count` to check the reference count."
msgstr "Gunakan `Rc::strong_count` untuk memeriksa reference count."

#: src/smart-pointers/rc.md
msgid ""
"`Rc::downgrade` gives you a _weakly reference-counted_ object to create "
"cycles that will be dropped properly (likely in combination with `RefCell`)."
msgstr ""
"`Rc::downgrade` memberikan objek dengan _weak reference counting_ untuk "
"membuat siklus yang tetap dapat di-drop dengan benar, biasanya bersama "
"`RefCell`."

#: src/smart-pointers/trait-objects.md
msgid ""
"We previously saw how trait objects can be used with references, e.g `&dyn "
"Pet`. However, we can also use trait objects with smart pointers like `Box` "
"to create an owned trait object: `Box<dyn Pet>`."
msgstr ""
"Sebelumnya, kita melihat penggunaan trait object dengan reference, misalnya "
"`&dyn Pet`. Trait object juga dapat digunakan bersama smart pointer seperti "
"`Box` untuk membuat owned trait object: `Box<dyn Pet>`."

