#: src/lifetimes.md
msgid "This segment should take about 1 hour and 5 minutes. It contains:"
msgstr ""
"Bagian ini diperkirakan membutuhkan waktu sekitar 1 jam dan 5 menit. Isinya:"

#: src/lifetimes/simple-borrows.md
msgid "Borrowing with Functions"
msgstr "Borrowing dengan Fungsi"

#: src/lifetimes/simple-borrows.md
msgid ""
"As part of borrow checking, the compiler needs to reason about how borrows "
"flow into and out of functions. In the simplest case borrows last for the "
"duration of the function call:"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai bagian dari borrow checking, compiler perlu menalar aliran borrow "
"yang masuk dan keluar dari fungsi. Dalam kasus paling sederhana, borrow "
"berlangsung selama pemanggilan fungsi:"

#: src/lifetimes/simple-borrows.md
msgid "// Borrow `val` for the function call.\n"
msgstr "// Borrow `val` for the function call.\n"

#: src/lifetimes/simple-borrows.md
msgid "// Borrow has ended and we're free to mutate.\n"
msgstr "// Borrow has ended and we're free to mutate.\n"

#: src/lifetimes/simple-borrows.md
msgid ""
"In this example we borrow `val` for the call to `borrows`. This would limit "
"our ability to mutate `val`, but once the function call returns the borrow "
"has ended and we're free to mutate again."
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, kita meminjam `val` untuk pemanggilan `borrows`. Ini "
"membatasi perubahan terhadap `val`, tetapi setelah pemanggilan fungsi "
"selesai, borrow berakhir dan nilainya boleh diubah kembali."

#: src/lifetimes/returning-borrows.md
msgid ""
"But we can also have our function return a reference! This means that a "
"borrow flows back out of a function:"
msgstr ""
"Namun, fungsi juga dapat mengembalikan reference! Artinya, borrow dapat "
"mengalir keluar kembali dari fungsi:"

#: src/lifetimes/returning-borrows.md
msgid "// x = 5; // 🛠️❌ `x` is still borrowed!\n"
msgstr "// x = 5; // 🛠️❌ `x` is still borrowed!\n"

#: src/lifetimes/returning-borrows.md
msgid ""
"Rust functions can return references, meaning that a borrow can flow back out "
"of a function."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi Rust dapat mengembalikan reference, sehingga borrow dapat mengalir "
"keluar kembali dari fungsi."

#: src/lifetimes/returning-borrows.md
msgid ""
"If a function returns a reference (or another kind of borrow), it was likely "
"derived from one of its arguments. This means that the return value of the "
"function will extend the borrow for one or more argument borrows."
msgstr ""
"Jika fungsi mengembalikan reference atau jenis borrow lain, kemungkinan "
"borrow itu berasal dari salah satu argumennya. Artinya, nilai kembalian "
"fungsi memperpanjang borrow pada satu atau beberapa argumen."

#: src/lifetimes/returning-borrows.md
msgid ""
"This case is still fairly simple, in that only one borrow is passed into the "
"function, so the returned borrow has to be the same one."
msgstr ""
"Kasus ini masih cukup sederhana karena hanya satu borrow diteruskan ke "
"fungsi, sehingga borrow yang dikembalikan harus berasal dari borrow yang sama."

#: src/lifetimes/multiple-borrows.md
msgid ""
"But what about when there are multiple borrows passed into a function and one "
"being returned?"
msgstr ""
"Bagaimana jika beberapa borrow diteruskan ke fungsi dan salah satunya "
"dikembalikan?"

#: src/lifetimes/multiple-borrows.md
msgid "\"Return either `a` or `b`\""
msgstr "\"Return either `a` or `b`\""

#: src/lifetimes/multiple-borrows.md
msgid ""
"// Which one is still borrowed?\n"
"    // Should either mutation be allowed?\n"
msgstr ""
"// Which one is still borrowed?\n"
"    // Should either mutation be allowed?\n"

#: src/lifetimes/multiple-borrows.md
msgid ""
"This code does not compile right now because it is missing lifetime "
"annotations. Before we get it to compile, use this opportunity to have "
"students to think about which of our argument borrows should be extended by "
"the return value."
msgstr ""
"Kode ini belum dapat dikompilasi karena tidak memiliki anotasi lifetime. "
"Sebelum memperbaikinya, ajak peserta memikirkan borrow argumen mana yang "
"seharusnya diperpanjang oleh nilai kembalian."

#: src/lifetimes/multiple-borrows.md
msgid ""
"We pass two borrows into `multiple` and one is going to come back out, which "
"means we will need to extend the borrow of one of the argument lifetimes. "
"Which one should be extended? Do we need to see the body of `multiple` to "
"figure this out?"
msgstr ""
"Kita meneruskan dua borrow ke `multiple` dan salah satunya dikembalikan, "
"sehingga lifetime borrow salah satu argumen perlu diperpanjang. Yang mana? "
"Apakah kita perlu melihat isi `multiple` untuk mengetahuinya?"

#: src/lifetimes/multiple-borrows.md
msgid ""
"When borrow checking, the compiler doesn't look at the body of `multiple` to "
"reason about the borrows flowing out, instead it looks only at the signature "
"of the function for borrow analysis."
msgstr ""
"Saat borrow checking, compiler tidak melihat isi `multiple` untuk menalar "
"borrow yang keluar. Analisis borrow hanya menggunakan signature fungsi."

#: src/lifetimes/multiple-borrows.md
msgid ""
"In this case there is not enough information to determine if `a` or `b` will "
"be borrowed by the returned reference. Show students the compiler errors and "
"introduce the lifetime syntax:"
msgstr ""
"Dalam kasus ini, informasinya tidak cukup untuk menentukan apakah reference "
"yang dikembalikan meminjam `a` atau `b`. Tunjukkan error compiler kepada "
"peserta dan perkenalkan sintaks lifetime:"

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-both.md
msgid ""
"In this case, we have a function where either `a` or `b` may be returned. In "
"this case we use the lifetime annotations to tell the compiler that both "
"borrows may flow into the return value."
msgstr ""
"Di sini, fungsi dapat mengembalikan `a` atau `b`. Kita menggunakan anotasi "
"lifetime untuk memberi tahu compiler bahwa kedua borrow mungkin mengalir ke "
"nilai kembalian."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-both.md
msgid ""
"// Which one is still borrowed?\n"
"    // Should either mutation be allowed?\n"
"    // a += 7;\n"
"    // b += 7;\n"
msgstr ""
"// Which one is still borrowed?\n"
"    // Should either mutation be allowed?\n"
"    // a += 7;\n"
"    // b += 7;\n"

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-both.md
msgid ""
"The `pick` function will return either `a` or `b` depending on the value of "
"`c`, which means we can't know at compile time which one will be returned."
msgstr ""
"Fungsi `pick` mengembalikan `a` atau `b` sesuai nilai `c`, sehingga kita "
"tidak dapat mengetahui saat compile time mana yang dikembalikan."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-both.md
msgid ""
"To express this to the compiler, we use the same lifetime for both `a` and "
"`b`, along with the return type. This means that the returned reference will "
"borrow BOTH `a` and `b`!"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menyatakannya kepada compiler, kita menggunakan lifetime yang sama pada "
"`a`, `b`, dan tipe nilai kembalian. Artinya, reference yang dikembalikan "
"meminjam KEDUANYA, baik `a` maupun `b`!"

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-both.md
msgid ""
"Uncomment both of the commented lines and show that `r` is borrowing both `a` "
"and `b`, even though at runtime it will only point to one of them."
msgstr ""
"Hapus penanda komentar pada kedua baris dan tunjukkan bahwa `r` meminjam `a` "
"dan `b`, meskipun saat runtime hanya merujuk salah satunya."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-both.md
msgid ""
"Change the first argument to `pick` to show that the result is the same "
"regardless of if `a` or `b` is returned."
msgstr ""
"Ubah argumen pertama `pick` untuk menunjukkan bahwa hasilnya tetap sama, baik "
"`a` maupun `b` yang dikembalikan."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid ""
"In this example `find_nearest` takes in multiple borrows but returns only one "
"of them. The lifetime annotations explicitly tie the returned borrow to the "
"corresponding argument borrow."
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh ini, `find_nearest` menerima beberapa borrow, tetapi hanya "
"mengembalikan salah satunya. Anotasi lifetime secara eksplisit mengaitkan "
"borrow yang dikembalikan dengan borrow argumen yang sesuai."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid ""
"/// Searches `points` for the point closest to `query`.\n"
"/// Assumes there's at least one point in `points`.\n"
msgstr ""
"/// Searches `points` for the point closest to `query`.\n"
"/// Assumes there's at least one point in `points`.\n"

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid "\"at least one point expected\""
msgstr "\"at least one point expected\""

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid "// query // What happens if we do this instead?\n"
msgstr "// query // What happens if we do this instead?\n"

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid "// `query` isn't borrowed at this point.\n"
msgstr "// `query` isn't borrowed at this point.\n"

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid ""
"It may be helpful to collapse the definition of `find_nearest` to put more "
"focus on the signature of the function. The actual logic in the function is "
"somewhat complex and isn't important for the purpose of borrow analysis."
msgstr ""
"Melipat tampilan definisi `find_nearest` dapat membantu memusatkan perhatian "
"pada signature fungsi. Logika di dalamnya agak kompleks dan tidak penting "
"untuk keperluan analisis borrow."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid ""
"When we call `find_nearest` the returned reference doesn't borrow `query`, "
"and so we are free to drop it while `nearest` is still active."
msgstr ""
"Ketika `find_nearest` dipanggil, reference yang dikembalikan tidak meminjam "
"`query`, sehingga nilainya boleh di-drop ketika `nearest` masih aktif."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid ""
"But what happens if we return the wrong borrow? Change the last line of "
"`find_nearest` to return `query` instead. Show the compiler error to the "
"students."
msgstr ""
"Apa yang terjadi jika kita mengembalikan borrow yang salah? Ubah baris "
"terakhir `find_nearest` agar mengembalikan `query`. Tunjukkan error compiler "
"kepada peserta."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid ""
"The first thing we have to do is add a lifetime annotation to `query`. Show "
"students that we can add a second lifetime `'b` to `find_nearest`."
msgstr ""
"Pertama, kita harus menambahkan anotasi lifetime pada `query`. Tunjukkan "
"bahwa lifetime kedua, `'b`, dapat ditambahkan ke `find_nearest`."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid ""
"Show the new error to the students. The borrow checker verifies that the "
"logic in the function body actually returns a reference with the correct "
"lifetime, enforcing that the function adheres to the contract set by the "
"function's signature."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan error baru kepada peserta. Borrow checker memverifikasi bahwa "
"logika dalam isi fungsi benar-benar mengembalikan reference dengan lifetime "
"yang tepat, sehingga fungsi mematuhi kontrak yang ditetapkan signature-nya."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid ""
"The \"help\" message in the error notes that we can add a lifetime bound `'b: "
"'a` to say that `'b` will live at least as long as `'a`, which would then "
"allow us to return `query`. This is an example of lifetime subtyping, which "
"allows us to return a longer lifetime where a shorter one is expected."
msgstr ""
"Pesan “help” pada error menjelaskan bahwa kita dapat menambahkan lifetime "
"bound `'b: 'a` untuk menyatakan bahwa `'b` berlaku setidaknya selama `'a`. "
"Dengan demikian, `query` boleh dikembalikan. Ini contoh lifetime subtyping, "
"yang memungkinkan lifetime lebih panjang dikembalikan ketika lifetime lebih "
"pendek diharapkan."

#: src/lifetimes/borrow-one.md
msgid ""
"We can do something similar by returning a `'static` lifetime, e.g., a "
"reference to a `static` variable. The `'static` lifetime is guaranteed to be "
"longer than any other lifetime, so it's always safe to return in place of a "
"shorter lifetime."
msgstr ""
"Hal serupa dapat dilakukan dengan mengembalikan lifetime `'static`, misalnya "
"reference ke variabel `static`. Lifetime `'static` dijamin lebih panjang "
"daripada lifetime lain, sehingga selalu aman dikembalikan sebagai pengganti "
"lifetime yang lebih pendek."

#: src/lifetimes/lifetime-elision.md
msgid ""
"Lifetimes for function argument and return types must be fully specified, but "
"Rust allows explicit lifetimes to be elided in most cases with [a few simple "
"rules](https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/lifetime-elision.html). This is not "
"inference -- it is just a syntactic shorthand."
msgstr ""
"Lifetime pada tipe argumen dan nilai kembalian fungsi harus ditentukan "
"sepenuhnya. Namun, Rust mengizinkan lifetime eksplisit dihilangkan dalam "
"sebagian besar kasus melalui [beberapa aturan sederhana](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/nomicon/lifetime-elision.html). Ini bukan inference, melainkan hanya "
"bentuk sintaks yang lebih singkat."

#: src/lifetimes/lifetime-elision.md
msgid "Each argument which does not have a lifetime annotation is given one."
msgstr ""
"Setiap argumen yang belum memiliki anotasi lifetime diberi satu lifetime."

#: src/lifetimes/lifetime-elision.md
msgid ""
"If there is only one argument lifetime, it is given to all un-annotated "
"borrows in the return type."
msgstr ""
"Jika hanya ada satu lifetime argumen, lifetime tersebut diberikan kepada "
"semua borrow tanpa anotasi pada tipe nilai kembalian."

#: src/lifetimes/lifetime-elision.md
msgid ""
"If there are multiple argument lifetimes, but the first one is for `self`, "
"that lifetime is given to all un-annotated borrows in the return type."
msgstr ""
"Jika ada beberapa lifetime argumen, tetapi yang pertama untuk `self`, "
"lifetime tersebut diberikan kepada semua borrow tanpa anotasi pada tipe nilai "
"kembalian."

#: src/lifetimes/lifetime-elision.md
msgid ""
"Walk through applying the lifetime elision rules to each of the example "
"functions. `only_args` is completed by the first rule, `identity` is "
"completed by the second, and `Foo::get` is completed by the third."
msgstr ""
"Jelaskan penerapan aturan lifetime elision pada setiap fungsi contoh. "
"`only_args` dilengkapi aturan pertama, `identity` oleh aturan kedua, dan "
"`Foo::get` oleh aturan ketiga."

#: src/lifetimes/lifetime-elision.md
msgid ""
"If all lifetimes have not been filled in by applying the three elision rules "
"then you will get a compiler error telling you to add annotations manually."
msgstr ""
"Jika ketiga aturan elision belum melengkapi seluruh lifetime, compiler akan "
"memberikan error yang meminta Anda menambahkan anotasi secara manual."

#: src/lifetimes/struct-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"If a data type stores borrowed data, it must be annotated with a lifetime:"
msgstr ""
"Jika tipe data menyimpan data pinjaman, tipe tersebut harus diberi anotasi "
"lifetime:"

#: src/lifetimes/struct-lifetimes.md
msgid "\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\""
msgstr "\"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\""

#: src/lifetimes/struct-lifetimes.md
msgid "// drop(doc);\n"
msgstr "// drop(doc);\n"

#: src/lifetimes/struct-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"In the above example, the annotation on `Highlight` enforces that the data "
"underlying the contained `&str` lives at least as long as any instance of "
"`Highlight` that uses that data. A struct cannot live longer than the data it "
"references."
msgstr ""
"Dalam contoh di atas, anotasi pada `Highlight` memastikan data yang mendasari "
"`&str` di dalamnya berlaku setidaknya selama setiap instance `Highlight` yang "
"menggunakannya. Struct tidak dapat berlaku lebih lama daripada data yang "
"dirujuk."

#: src/lifetimes/struct-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"If `doc` is dropped before the end of the lifetime of `noun` or `verb`, the "
"borrow checker throws an error."
msgstr ""
"Jika `doc` di-drop sebelum lifetime `noun` atau `verb` berakhir, borrow "
"checker memberikan error."

#: src/lifetimes/struct-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"Types with borrowed data force users to hold on to the original data. This "
"can be useful for creating lightweight views, but it generally makes them "
"somewhat harder to use."
msgstr ""
"Tipe dengan data pinjaman mengharuskan pengguna mempertahankan data asal. Ini "
"berguna untuk membuat view ringan, tetapi umumnya membuat penggunaannya agak "
"lebih sulit."

#: src/lifetimes/struct-lifetimes.md
msgid "When possible, make data structures own their data directly."
msgstr ""
"Jika memungkinkan, buat struktur data memiliki ownership langsung atas "
"datanya."

#: src/lifetimes/struct-lifetimes.md
msgid ""
"Some structs with multiple references inside can have more than one lifetime "
"annotation. This can be necessary if there is a need to describe lifetime "
"relationships between the references themselves, in addition to the lifetime "
"of the struct itself. Those are very advanced use cases."
msgstr ""
"Struct yang memuat beberapa reference dapat memiliki lebih dari satu anotasi "
"lifetime. Ini mungkin diperlukan untuk menjelaskan hubungan lifetime antar-"
"reference, selain lifetime struct itu sendiri. Kasus penggunaan ini sangat "
"lanjut."

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid ""
"In this exercise, you will build a parser for the [protobuf binary encoding]"
"(https://protobuf.dev/programming-guides/encoding/). Don't worry, it's "
"simpler than it seems! This illustrates a common parsing pattern, passing "
"slices of data. The underlying data itself is never copied."
msgstr ""
"Dalam latihan ini, Anda membuat parser untuk [encoding biner protobuf]"
"(https://protobuf.dev/programming-guides/encoding/). Jangan khawatir, ini "
"lebih sederhana daripada kelihatannya! Latihan ini menunjukkan pola parsing "
"umum, yaitu meneruskan slice data. Data yang mendasarinya tidak pernah "
"disalin."

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Fully parsing a protobuf message requires knowing the types of the fields, "
"indexed by their field numbers. That is typically provided in a `proto` file. "
"In this exercise, we'll encode that information into `match` statements in "
"functions that get called for each field."
msgstr ""
"Parsing pesan protobuf secara lengkap memerlukan informasi tipe field "
"berdasarkan nomor field-nya. Informasi ini biasanya tersedia dalam berkas "
"`proto`. Dalam latihan ini, kita menyatakannya melalui statement `match` pada "
"fungsi yang dipanggil untuk setiap field."

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid "We'll use the following proto:"
msgstr "Kita menggunakan proto berikut:"

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid "Messages"
msgstr "Pesan"

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid ""
"A proto message is encoded as a series of fields, one after the next. Each is "
"implemented as a \"tag\" followed by the value. The tag contains a field "
"number (e.g., `2` for the `id` field of a `Person` message) and a wire type "
"defining how the payload should be determined from the byte stream. These are "
"combined into a single integer, as decoded in `unpack_tag` below."
msgstr ""
"Pesan proto dienkode sebagai rangkaian field yang berurutan. Setiap field "
"berupa “tag” diikuti nilai. Tag memuat nomor field, misalnya `2` untuk field "
"`id` pada pesan `Person`, dan wire type yang menentukan cara memperoleh "
"payload dari byte stream. Keduanya digabungkan menjadi satu integer, seperti "
"yang didekode dalam `unpack_tag` berikut."

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid "Varint"
msgstr "Varint"

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Integers, including the tag, are represented with a variable-length encoding "
"called VARINT. Luckily, `parse_varint` is defined for you below."
msgstr ""
"Integer, termasuk tag, direpresentasikan dengan encoding berpanjang variabel "
"yang disebut VARINT. Untungnya, `parse_varint` sudah disediakan untuk Anda di "
"bawah."

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid "Wire Types"
msgstr "Wire Type"

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid ""
"Proto defines several wire types, only two of which are used in this exercise."
msgstr ""
"Proto mendefinisikan beberapa wire type, tetapi hanya dua yang digunakan "
"dalam latihan ini."

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The `Varint` wire type contains a single varint, and is used to encode proto "
"values of type `int32` such as `Person.id`."
msgstr ""
"Wire type `Varint` memuat satu varint dan digunakan untuk mengenkode nilai "
"proto bertipe `int32`, seperti `Person.id`."

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The `Len` wire type contains a length expressed as a varint, followed by a "
"payload of that number of bytes. This is used to encode proto values of type "
"`string` such as `Person.name`. It is also used to encode proto values "
"containing sub-messages such as `Person.phones`, where the payload contains "
"an encoding of the sub-message."
msgstr ""
"Wire type `Len` memuat panjang yang dinyatakan sebagai varint, diikuti "
"payload dengan jumlah byte tersebut. Bentuk ini mengenkode nilai proto "
"bertipe `string`, seperti `Person.name`. Bentuk ini juga mengenkode nilai "
"proto yang memuat subpesan, seperti `Person.phones`, dengan payload berupa "
"encoding subpesan tersebut."

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid ""
"The given code also defines callbacks to handle `Person` and `PhoneNumber` "
"fields, and to parse a message into a series of calls to those callbacks."
msgstr ""
"Kode yang tersedia juga mendefinisikan callback untuk menangani field "
"`Person` dan `PhoneNumber`, serta melakukan parsing pesan menjadi rangkaian "
"pemanggilan callback tersebut."

#: src/lifetimes/exercise.md
msgid ""
"What remains for you is to implement the `parse_field` function and the "
"`ProtoMessage` trait for `Person` and `PhoneNumber`."
msgstr ""
"Tugas Anda adalah mengimplementasikan fungsi `parse_field` dan trait "
"`ProtoMessage` untuk `Person` dan `PhoneNumber`."

