#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid "Motivating Iterators"
msgstr "Alasan Menggunakan Iterator"

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"If you want to iterate over the contents of an array, you'll need to define:"
msgstr "Untuk mengiterasi isi array, Anda perlu menentukan:"

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"Some state to keep track of where you are in the iteration process, e.g. an "
"index."
msgstr "State untuk mencatat posisi dalam proses iterasi, misalnya indeks."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid "A condition to determine when iteration is done."
msgstr "Kondisi untuk menentukan kapan iterasi selesai."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid "Logic for updating the state of iteration each loop."
msgstr "Logika untuk memperbarui state iterasi setiap putaran."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid "Logic for fetching each element using that iteration state."
msgstr "Logika untuk mengambil setiap elemen berdasarkan state iterasi."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid "In a C-style for loop you declare these things directly:"
msgstr "Dalam for loop bergaya C, semua hal ini dideklarasikan langsung:"

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"In Rust we bundle this state and logic together into an object known as an "
"\"iterator\"."
msgstr ""
"Dalam Rust, state dan logika tersebut digabungkan ke dalam objek yang disebut "
"“iterator”."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"This slide provides context for what Rust iterators do under the hood. We use "
"the (hopefully) familiar construct of a C-style `for` loop to show how "
"iteration requires some state and some logic, that way on the next slide we "
"can show how an iterator bundles these together."
msgstr ""
"Slide ini memberi konteks tentang cara kerja iterator Rust di balik layar. "
"Kita menggunakan loop `for` bergaya C yang diharapkan sudah familier untuk "
"menunjukkan bahwa iterasi memerlukan state dan logika. Pada slide berikutnya, "
"kita dapat menunjukkan cara iterator menggabungkan keduanya."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"Rust doesn't have a C-style `for` loop, but we can express the same thing "
"with `while`:"
msgstr ""
"Rust tidak memiliki loop `for` bergaya C, tetapi hal yang sama dapat "
"dinyatakan menggunakan `while`:"

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"There's another way to express array iteration using `for` in C and C++: You "
"can use a pointer to the front and a pointer to the end of the array and then "
"compare those pointers to determine when the loop should end."
msgstr ""
"Ada cara lain untuk menyatakan iterasi array menggunakan `for` dalam C dan C+"
"+: gunakan pointer ke awal dan akhir array, lalu bandingkan keduanya untuk "
"menentukan kapan loop berakhir."

#: src/iterators/motivation.md
msgid ""
"If students ask, you can point out that this is how Rust's slice and array "
"iterators work under the hood (though implemented as a Rust iterator)."
msgstr ""
"Jika peserta bertanya, sampaikan bahwa beginilah cara kerja iterator slice "
"dan array Rust di balik layar, meskipun diimplementasikan sebagai iterator "
"Rust."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"The [`Iterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html) "
"trait defines how an object can be used to produce a sequence of values. For "
"example, if we wanted to create an iterator that can produce the elements of "
"a slice it might look something like this:"
msgstr ""
"Trait [`Iterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html) "
"mendefinisikan cara objek menghasilkan rangkaian nilai. Misalnya, iterator "
"yang menghasilkan elemen slice dapat berbentuk seperti berikut:"

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"The `SliceIter` example implements the same logic as the C-style `for` loop "
"demonstrated on the last slide."
msgstr ""
"Contoh `SliceIter` mengimplementasikan logika yang sama dengan loop `for` "
"bergaya C pada slide sebelumnya."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"Point out to the students that iterators are lazy: Creating the iterator just "
"initializes the struct but does not otherwise do any work. No work happens "
"until the `next` method is called."
msgstr ""
"Sampaikan bahwa iterator bersifat lazy: pembuatannya hanya menginisialisasi "
"struct, tanpa melakukan pekerjaan lain. Pekerjaan baru dilakukan ketika "
"method `next` dipanggil."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"Iterators don't need to be finite! It's entirely valid to have an iterator "
"that will produce values forever. For example, a half open range like `0..` "
"will keep going until integer overflow occurs."
msgstr ""
"Iterator tidak harus berhingga! Iterator yang terus menghasilkan nilai tetap "
"valid. Misalnya, rentang terbuka di salah satu sisi seperti `0..` terus "
"berjalan sampai terjadi integer overflow."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"The \"real\" version of `SliceIter` is the [`slice::Iter`](https://doc.rust-"
"lang.org/stable/std/slice/struct.Iter.html) type in the standard library, "
"however the real version uses pointers under the hood instead of an index in "
"order to eliminate bounds checks."
msgstr ""
"Versi “sebenarnya” dari `SliceIter` adalah tipe [`slice::Iter`](https://"
"doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/slice/struct.Iter.html) dalam standard library. "
"Namun, versi ini menggunakan pointer, bukan indeks, untuk menghilangkan "
"pemeriksaan batas."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"The `SliceIter` example is a good example of a struct that contains a "
"reference and therefore uses lifetime annotations."
msgstr ""
"`SliceIter` merupakan contoh yang baik dari struct yang memuat reference, "
"sehingga menggunakan anotasi lifetime."

#: src/iterators/iterator.md
msgid ""
"You can also demonstrate adding a generic parameter to `SliceIter` to allow "
"it to work with any kind of slice (not just `&[i32]`)."
msgstr ""
"Anda juga dapat memperagakan penambahan parameter generic pada `SliceIter` "
"agar dapat digunakan pada slice bertipe apa pun, bukan hanya `&[i32]`."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"In addition to the `next` method that defines how an iterator behaves, the "
"`Iterator` trait provides 70+ helper methods that can be used to build "
"customized iterators."
msgstr ""
"Selain method `next` yang menentukan perilaku iterator, trait `Iterator` "
"menyediakan 70+ method bantu untuk membuat iterator sesuai kebutuhan."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid "// Create a range from 1 to 10\n"
msgstr "// Create a range from 1 to 10\n"

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid "// Keep only even numbers\n"
msgstr "// Keep only even numbers\n"

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid "// Square each number\n"
msgstr "// Square each number\n"

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid "// Sum up all the squared numbers\n"
msgstr "// Sum up all the squared numbers\n"

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid "\"The sum of squares of even numbers from 1 to 10 is: {}\""
msgstr "\"The sum of squares of even numbers from 1 to 10 is: {}\""

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"The `Iterator` trait implements many common functional programming operations "
"over collections (e.g. `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, etc). This is the trait "
"where you can find all the documentation about them."
msgstr ""
"Trait `Iterator` mengimplementasikan banyak operasi pemrograman fungsional "
"yang umum pada collection, seperti `map`, `filter`, `reduce`, dan lainnya. "
"Seluruh dokumentasinya dapat ditemukan pada trait ini."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"Many of these helper methods take the original iterator and produce a new "
"iterator with different behavior. These are know as \"iterator adapter "
"methods\"."
msgstr ""
"Banyak method bantu menerima iterator asal dan menghasilkan iterator baru "
"dengan perilaku berbeda. Method ini dikenal sebagai “iterator adapter method”."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"Some methods, like `sum` and `count`, consume the iterator and pull all of "
"the elements out of it."
msgstr ""
"Sebagian method, seperti `sum` dan `count`, mengonsumsi iterator dan "
"mengambil seluruh elemennya."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"These methods are designed to be chained together so that it's easy to build "
"a custom iterator that does exactly what you need."
msgstr ""
"Method-method ini dirancang untuk dirangkai agar mudah membuat iterator "
"khusus yang melakukan tepat apa yang Anda butuhkan."

#: src/iterators/helpers.md
msgid ""
"Rust's iterators are extremely efficient and highly optimizable. Even complex "
"iterators made by combining many adapter methods will still result in code as "
"efficient as equivalent imperative implementations."
msgstr ""
"Iterator Rust sangat efisien dan mudah dioptimalkan. Bahkan iterator kompleks "
"yang menggabungkan banyak adapter method tetap menghasilkan kode seefisien "
"implementasi imperatif yang setara."

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid ""
"The [`enumerate`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/iter/"
"trait.Iterator.html#method.enumerate) helper gives us a way to get the index "
"of each element for any iterator."
msgstr ""
"Method bantu [`enumerate`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/std/iter/"
"trait.Iterator.html#method.enumerate) menyediakan cara mendapatkan indeks "
"setiap elemen pada iterator apa pun."

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "'b'"
msgstr "'b'"

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "'c'"
msgstr "'c'"

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "'e'"
msgstr "'e'"

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "// By default iterating over an array just gives its elements.\n"
msgstr "// By default iterating over an array just gives its elements.\n"

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "\"The element is {letter:?}, but what's its index?\""
msgstr "\"The element is {letter:?}, but what's its index?\""

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "// `enumerate` gives both the element and its index.\n"
msgstr "// `enumerate` gives both the element and its index.\n"

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid "\"{letter:?} has index {i}\""
msgstr "\"{letter:?} has index {i}\""

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid ""
"A nuance of Rust's iterators and `for` loops is that an iterator by default "
"does not give you the index of each element. This is fine when all you need "
"are e.g. the values in an array, but it's common to also want the index of "
"each element as you iterate."
msgstr ""
"Salah satu detail iterator Rust dan loop `for` adalah bahwa secara default "
"iterator tidak memberikan indeks setiap elemen. Ini cukup jika Anda hanya "
"memerlukan nilai dalam array, tetapi sering kali indeks setiap elemen juga "
"diperlukan saat iterasi."

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid ""
"`enumerate` creates an iterator that produces a tuple where the first element "
"is the index and the second element is the original iterator's item."
msgstr ""
"`enumerate` membuat iterator yang menghasilkan tuple dengan indeks sebagai "
"elemen pertama dan item iterator asal sebagai elemen kedua."

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid ""
"Point out that we can use a pattern for the loop variable in a `for` loop. "
"This allows us to destructure the tuple produced by `enumerate`."
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan bahwa pattern dapat digunakan untuk variabel loop `for`. Dengan "
"demikian, kita dapat melakukan destructuring tuple yang dihasilkan "
"`enumerate`."

#: src/iterators/enumerate.md
msgid ""
"Note that we had to do `.iter()` first; `enumerate` is an iterator method, "
"not a method on the array type itself."
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa kita harus memanggil `.iter()` lebih dahulu: `enumerate` "
"merupakan method iterator, bukan method tipe array itu sendiri."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"The [`collect`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/"
"trait.Iterator.html#method.collect) method lets you build a collection from "
"an [`Iterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html)."
msgstr ""
"Method [`collect`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/"
"trait.Iterator.html#method.collect) memungkinkan pembuatan collection dari "
"[`Iterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.Iterator.html)."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid "\"prime_squares: {prime_squares:?}\""
msgstr "\"prime_squares: {prime_squares:?}\""

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"Any iterator can be collected in to a `Vec`, `VecDeque`, or `HashSet`. "
"Iterators that produce key-value pairs (i.e. a two-element tuple) can also be "
"collected into `HashMap` and `BTreeMap`."
msgstr ""
"Iterator apa pun dapat dikumpulkan menjadi `Vec`, `VecDeque`, atau `HashSet`. "
"Iterator yang menghasilkan pasangan key-value, yaitu tuple berisi dua elemen, "
"juga dapat dikumpulkan menjadi `HashMap` dan `BTreeMap`."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"Show the students the definition for `collect` in the standard library docs. "
"There are two ways to specify the generic type `B` for this method:"
msgstr ""
"Tunjukkan definisi `collect` dalam dokumentasi standard library kepada "
"peserta. Ada dua cara menentukan tipe generic `B` untuk method ini:"

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"With the \"turbofish\": `some_iterator.collect::<COLLECTION_TYPE>()`, as "
"shown. The `_` shorthand used here lets Rust infer the type of the `Vec` "
"elements."
msgstr ""
"Dengan “turbofish”: `some_iterator.collect::<COLLECTION_TYPE>()`, seperti "
"pada contoh. Bentuk singkat `_` memungkinkan Rust menyimpulkan tipe elemen "
"`Vec`."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"With type inference: `let prime_squares: Vec<_> = some_iterator.collect()`. "
"Rewrite the example to use this form."
msgstr ""
"Dengan type inference: `let prime_squares: Vec<_> = some_iterator.collect()`. "
"Tulis ulang contoh menggunakan bentuk ini."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"If students are curious about how this works, you can bring up the "
"[`FromIterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.FromIterator.html) "
"trait, which defines how each type of collection gets built from an iterator."
msgstr ""
"Jika peserta ingin mengetahui cara kerjanya, tunjukkan trait [`FromIterator`]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/trait.FromIterator.html), yang "
"mendefinisikan cara setiap tipe collection dibuat dari iterator."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"In addition to the basic implementations of `FromIterator` for `Vec`, "
"`HashMap`, etc., there are also more specialized implementations which let "
"you do cool things like convert an `Iterator<Item = Result<V, E>>` into a "
"`Result<Vec<V>, E>`."
msgstr ""
"Selain implementasi dasar `FromIterator` untuk `Vec`, `HashMap`, dan lainnya, "
"ada implementasi yang lebih khusus untuk hal menarik seperti mengonversi "
"`Iterator<Item = Result<V, E>>` menjadi `Result<Vec<V>, E>`."

#: src/iterators/collect.md
msgid ""
"The reason type annotations are often needed with `collect` is because it's "
"generic over its return type. This makes it harder for the compiler to infer "
"the correct type in many cases."
msgstr ""
"Anotasi tipe sering diperlukan pada `collect` karena tipe nilai kembaliannya "
"bersifat generic. Dalam banyak kasus, ini mempersulit compiler menyimpulkan "
"tipe yang tepat."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid ""
"The `Iterator` trait tells you how to _iterate_ once you have created an "
"iterator. The related trait [`IntoIterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/"
"iter/trait.IntoIterator.html) defines how to create an iterator for a type. "
"It is used automatically by the `for` loop."
msgstr ""
"Trait `Iterator` menentukan cara _mengiterasi_ setelah iterator dibuat. Trait "
"terkait, [`IntoIterator`](https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/iter/"
"trait.IntoIterator.html), mendefinisikan cara membuat iterator bagi suatu "
"tipe. Trait ini digunakan otomatis oleh loop `for`."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid "\"point = {x}, {y}\""
msgstr "\"point = {x}, {y}\""

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid "// dbg!(&grid.x_coords); // ❌ The grid was consumed by the loop.\n"
msgstr "// dbg!(&grid.x_coords); // ❌ The grid was consumed by the loop.\n"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid ""
"`IntoIterator` is the trait that makes for loops work. It is implemented by "
"collection types such as `Vec<T>` and references to them such as `&Vec<T>` "
"and `&[T]`. Ranges also implement it. This is why you can iterate over a "
"vector with `for i in some_vec { .. }` but `some_vec.next()` doesn't exist."
msgstr ""
"`IntoIterator` merupakan trait yang memungkinkan for loop bekerja. Tipe "
"collection seperti `Vec<T>` dan reference-nya, seperti `&Vec<T>` dan `&[T]`, "
"mengimplementasikan trait ini. Rentang juga mengimplementasikannya. Karena "
"itu, Anda dapat mengiterasi vector menggunakan `for i in some_vec { .. }`, "
"meskipun `some_vec.next()` tidak tersedia."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid ""
"Click through to the docs for `IntoIterator`. Every implementation of "
"`IntoIterator` must declare two types:"
msgstr ""
"Buka dokumentasi `IntoIterator`. Setiap implementasi `IntoIterator` harus "
"mendeklarasikan dua tipe:"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid "`Item`: the type to iterate over, such as `i8`,"
msgstr "`Item`: tipe yang diiterasi, misalnya `i8`,"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid "`IntoIter`: the `Iterator` type returned by the `into_iter` method."
msgstr "`IntoIter`: tipe `Iterator` yang dikembalikan method `into_iter`."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid ""
"Note that `IntoIter` and `Item` are linked: the iterator must have the same "
"`Item` type, which means that it returns `Option<Item>`"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa `IntoIter` dan `Item` saling terkait: iterator harus "
"memiliki tipe `Item` yang sama, sehingga mengembalikan `Option<Item>`"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid "The example iterates over all combinations of x and y coordinates."
msgstr "Contoh ini mengiterasi semua kombinasi koordinat x dan y."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator.md
msgid ""
"Uncomment the commented line in `main` and show the compiler error. Note that "
"`IntoIterator::into_iter` takes ownership of `self`. The next slide shows how "
"we can avoid this by iterating over `&Grid` with an additional `IntoIterator` "
"implementation."
msgstr ""
"Hapus penanda komentar pada baris di `main` dan tampilkan error compiler. "
"Perhatikan bahwa `IntoIterator::into_iter` mengambil ownership atas `self`. "
"Slide berikutnya menunjukkan cara menghindarinya dengan mengiterasi `&Grid` "
"melalui implementasi `IntoIterator` tambahan."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid ""
"Implementing `IntoIterator` directly on a type means that creating the "
"iterator takes ownership of the object, so a common pattern is to implement "
"it on a reference to allow for the creation of borrowing iterators."
msgstr ""
"Mengimplementasikan `IntoIterator` langsung pada tipe berarti pembuatan "
"iterator mengambil ownership objek. Karena itu, pola yang umum adalah "
"mengimplementasikannya pada reference agar dapat membuat borrowing iterator."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid "// The loop can borrow the grid without taking ownership.\n"
msgstr "// The loop can borrow the grid without taking ownership.\n"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid "// The grid remains accessible after the loop.\n"
msgstr "// The grid remains accessible after the loop.\n"

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid ""
"By implementing `IntoIterator` on `&Grid`, we can pass a reference into a "
"`for` loop and get a borrowing iterator. This allows us to borrow the grid "
"object in the loop without taking ownership of it."
msgstr ""
"Dengan mengimplementasikan `IntoIterator` pada `&Grid`, kita dapat meneruskan "
"reference ke loop `for` dan memperoleh borrowing iterator. Dengan demikian, "
"loop dapat meminjam objek grid tanpa mengambil ownership."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid ""
"[This playground](https://play.rust-lang.org/?"
"version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=c3c29974bac8cc2065ca1b6608d5c8b9) "
"shows that we can have both `GridIter` and `GridRefIter` at the same time."
msgstr ""
"[Playground ini](https://play.rust-lang.org/?"
"version=stable&mode=debug&edition=2024&gist=c3c29974bac8cc2065ca1b6608d5c8b9) "
"menunjukkan bahwa kita dapat memiliki `GridIter` dan `GridRefIter` sekaligus."

#: src/iterators/intoiterator-refs.md
msgid ""
"This pattern is used heavily in the standard library for its collection "
"types, allowing for owning and borrowing iterators to be created implicitly "
"based on whether you pass the object in by value, by reference, or by mutable "
"reference."
msgstr ""
"Pola ini banyak digunakan pada tipe collection dalam standard library. Owning "
"iterator dan borrowing iterator dapat dibuat secara implisit sesuai cara "
"objek diteruskan: by value, by reference, atau melalui mutable reference."

